var e={"p ← partition(a)        // as in quick sort":`p ← partition(a)        // 和快速排序一樣`,"if p = k: return a[p]":`如果 p = k: 返回 a[p]`,"if k < p:":`如果 k < p:`,"return select(the part before p, k)":`返回 select(p 之前的部分, k)`,"return select(the part after p, k)":`返回 select(p 之後的部分, k)`,"One item, not the whole order":`一項，而不是整個順序`,"Which is the 2nd smallest of these? Or the median? You could sort the row and read off the cell, but that does far more work than the question asks for.":`這些數中第 2 小的是哪個？或者中位數？你可以把這一排排好序再讀出那個格子，但那樣做的工作遠超問題所需。`,"In a sorted row the 2nd smallest sits in cell 1. The only thing that matters is what ends up in that one cell.":`在排好序的一排裡，第 2 小的在格子 1。唯一重要的是最後落在那一個格子裡的是什麼。`,"what belongs here?":`這裡該放什麼？`,"Looking for":`要找的是`,"the 2nd smallest":`第 2 小的`,"cell 1":`格子 1`,"Pivot landed in":`基準落在`,"Still searching":`仍在搜尋`,"cells 0 to 7":`格子 0 到 7`,"Items looked at":`檢視過的項`,"Partition once":`劃分一次`,"Do one quick sort partition around the last item, 4. Smaller items go to its left, bigger to its right, and 4 drops into cell 3.":`圍繞最後一項 4 做一次快速排序的劃分。更小的項去它左邊，更大的去右邊，4 落到格子 3。`,"That is 4’s final cell. So 4 is the 4th smallest, without anything having been sorted.":`那是 4 的最終位置。所以 4 是第 4 小的，而什麼都還沒排序。`,"the 4th smallest":`第 4 小的`,"cell 3":`格子 3`,"Throw one side away":`扔掉一邊`,"Cell 1 is to the left of cell 3. So the answer is one of the three items on the left.":`格子 1 在格子 3 的左邊。所以答案是左邊三項之一。`,"Quick sort would now sort <em>both</em> sides. Quickselect drops the right side for good: five items it will never look at again.":`快速排序這時會把<em>兩邊</em>都排好。快速選擇則永久丟掉右邊：五個它再也不會看的項。`,"it is in here":`在這裡面`,"cells 0 to 2":`格子 0 到 2`,"Partition what is left":`劃分剩下的`,"Same again on those three, around the last one, 1. Nothing is smaller, so 1 swaps into cell 0.":`對這三項再做一次，圍繞最後一項 1。沒有更小的，所以 1 交換到格子 0。`,"Cell 1 is to its right this time. Two items left.":`這次格子 1 在它右邊。剩下兩項。`,"cell 0":`格子 0`,"cells 1 to 2":`格子 1 到 2`,"The pivot lands on the cell":`基準落在了那個格子上`,"Partition the last two around 2. It swaps into cell 1: exactly the cell being asked about.":`圍繞 2 劃分最後兩項。它交換到格子 1：正好是問的那個格子。`,"The 2nd smallest is 2. The right side of the row is still a jumble, and it does not matter.":`第 2 小的是 2。這一排的右邊還是亂的，但這無所謂。`,"2nd smallest":`第 2 小的`,found:`找到了`,"Half the work each time":`每次只做一半的工作`,"Each round looks only at what survived the last: 8 items, then 3, then 2. On average the pile halves, and n + n/2 + n/4 + … never reaches 2n.":`每一輪只看上一輪留下來的：8 項，然後 3 項，然後 2 項。平均下來，剩下的每次減半，而 n + n/2 + n/4 + … 永遠不會達到 2n。`,"Like quick sort, a run of bad pivots makes it slow. Picking the pivot at random makes that very unlikely.":`和快速排序一樣，一連串糟糕的基準會讓它變慢。隨機選基準能讓這非常不可能發生。`,"O(n) on average, against O(n log n) to sort first. O(n²) at worst.":`平均 O(n)，而先排序要 O(n log n)。最壞 O(n²)。`,"Sorting would have looked at about 24.":`排序的話大約要看 24 次。`},t={"subsets(items, chosen so far):":`subsets(items, chosen):`,"if no items are left:":`如果 沒有剩下的項:`,"record chosen":`記錄 chosen`,"take the next item":`取下一項`,"subsets(the rest, chosen + that item)":`subsets(其餘的, chosen + 這一項)`,"put it back                    // undo the choice":`把它放回去                    // 撤銷這個選擇`,"subsets(the rest, chosen)":`subsets(其餘的, chosen)`,"Choices made":`已做的選擇`,"Every possible choice":`每一種可能的選擇`,"List every subset of A, B, C: every way of choosing some, all or none of them. Many problems come down to this: try every combination, and keep the ones that work.":`列出 A、B、C 的每個子集：選其中一些、全部或一個都不選的每一種方式。很多問題都歸結於此：試遍每種組合，留下行得通的。`,"<strong>Backtracking</strong> is the organised way to do it. Start with nothing chosen.":`<strong>回溯</strong>是有條理地做這件事的方法。從什麼都沒選開始。`,"nothing chosen yet":`還什麼都沒選`,"Items decided":`已決定的項`,"of A, B, C":`/ A、B、C`,"Subsets found":`已找到的子集`,"One decision at a time":`一次一個決定`,Choose:`選擇`,"Take the first item and make one decision about it: is A in, or out? Each answer leads somewhere different.":`取第一項，對它做一個決定：A 要還是不要？每個回答都通向不同的地方。`,"Going left means taking it. Going right means leaving it.":`往左表示要它。往右表示不要它。`,"A tree of choices":`一棵選擇樹`,"From each of those, decide about B in the same way. Then C. Every decision doubles the number of ways things could have gone.":`對每個分支，用同樣的方式決定 B。然後是 C。每個決定都讓可能的走向翻倍。`,"The leaves are the answers":`葉子就是答案`,"After three decisions there is nothing left to decide. Each leaf is one complete set of choices: one subset. There are eight, from ABC to the empty set.":`三個決定之後，就沒有什麼要決定的了。每片葉子都是一組完整的選擇：一個子集。一共八個，從 ABC 到空集。`,"No subset is missed and none appears twice, because every leaf is reached by a different run of decisions.":`沒有子集被遺漏，也沒有出現兩次的，因為每片葉子都是由一串不同的決定到達的。`,"Walking it: go back and try again":`走一遍：退回去再試`,"The tree is never built in memory. A recursive function walks it depth first: go down taking items until a leaf, record it, then step <strong>back</strong> one decision, undo it, and take the other branch.":`這棵樹從來不會在記憶體中構建出來。一個遞迴函式深度優先地走它：一路取項往下走到一片葉子，記錄下來，然後<strong>退回</strong>一個決定，撤銷它，走另一個分支。`,"That step back is the backtrack. Only the current path is ever held.":`那一步退回就是回溯。任何時候只儲存當前的路徑。`,"n items have 2ⁿ subsets. Backtracking pays off when whole branches can be ruled out early, as in the next lesson.":`n 個項有 2ⁿ 個子集。當整個分支能被提前排除時，回溯才划算，就像下一課那樣。`,"Numbered in the order they are reached.":`按到達的順序編號。`},n={"if nothing is unused:":`如果 沒有未使用的:`,"record the arrangement":`記錄 這個排列`,"for each item in unused:":`對每個 unused 中的項:`,"move it onto the end of arrangement   // choose":`把它移到 arrangement 的末尾   // 選擇`,"permute(arrangement, the rest)        // explore":`permute(arrangement, 其餘的)        // 探索`,"move it back                          // un-choose":`把它移回去                          // 撤銷選擇`,Arrangements:`排列`,"Every possible order":`每一種可能的順序`,"Three letters wait in the row behind. In how many different orders can they be laid out in front? Each order is a <strong>permutation</strong>.":`後面一排有三個字母在等著。它們在前面能排成多少種不同的順序？每種順序都是一個<strong>排列</strong>。`,"There are 3 choices for the first place, 2 left for the second, 1 for the third: 3 × 2 × 1 = 6. The job is to produce all six without missing or repeating one.":`第一個位置有 3 種選擇，第二個剩 2 種，第三個 1 種：3 × 2 × 1 = 6。任務是把六種全部列出來，不漏也不重複。`,"Found so far":`目前已找到`,"Choose, then choose again":`選擇，再選擇`,"Fill the places from the left, always taking the first unused letter. A goes first. Of what is left, B goes second. Only C remains for the third.":`從左往右填位置，每次都取第一個未使用的字母。A 排第一。剩下的裡面，B 排第二。第三個只剩 C 了。`,"Nothing is unused, so this is a complete arrangement: A B C.":`沒有未使用的了，所以這是一個完整的排列：A B C。`,"Undo the last choices":`撤銷最後的選擇`,"To get a different arrangement, take the last choice back. C comes off, but it was the only option for the third place. So B comes off too.":`要得到不同的排列，就收回最後一個選擇。C 拿下來，但它是第三個位置唯一的選項。所以 B 也拿下來。`,"A stays where it is. The second place still has one option that has not been tried: C.":`A 留在原處。第二個位置還有一個沒試過的選項：C。`,"B is done here: try C":`B 在這裡已試過：試 C`,"Try the next option":`試下一個選項`,"C goes second this time, and B is all that is left for the third. A C B.":`這次 C 排第二，第三個只剩 B。A C B。`,"That is everything that starts with A.":`以 A 開頭的就是這些了。`,"Back all the way":`一路退回去`,"Both options for the second place have been used, so the search backs up past it. Even A comes off.":`第二個位置的兩個選項都用過了，所以搜尋退過它。連 A 也拿下來了。`,"The first place has two options it has not tried yet.":`第一個位置還有兩個沒試過的選項。`,"A is done here: try B":`A 在這裡已試過：試 B`,"A new first letter":`新的第一個字母`,"B goes first. The rest goes exactly as before, on the letters that are left: A then C gives B A C, and backing up one gives B C A.":`B 排第一。剩下的完全和之前一樣，用剩下的字母來排：A 然後 C 得到 B A C，退回一步得到 B C A。`,"B C A comes next.":`接下來是 B C A。`,"Choose, explore, un-choose":`選擇、探索、撤銷選擇`,"With C first come C A B and C B A, and the search is over: six arrangements, each found once.":`C 排第一時得到 C A B 和 C B A，搜尋結束：六個排列，每個只找到一次。`,"This is the whole shape of backtracking. Make a choice, follow it as far as it goes, then put things back exactly as they were and make the next choice.":`這就是回溯的完整形狀。做一個選擇，順著它走到底，然後把東西原樣放回去，再做下一個選擇。`,"n! arrangements. 10 items make 3.6 million; 15 make over a trillion.":`n! 個排列。10 個項有 360 萬個；15 個就超過一萬億個。`},r={"if square is the exit: return yes":`如果 square 是出口: 返回 是`,"put square on the trail":`把 square 放到足跡上`,"for each neighbour: right, forward, left, back:":`對每個 鄰居，按右、前、左、後:`,"if it is open and not on the trail:":`如果 它是通的且不在足跡上:`,"if solve(neighbour): return yes":`如果 solve(neighbour): 返回 是`,"take square off the trail      // dead end":`把 square 從足跡上拿下      // 死路`,"The walk":`行走`,"A way through":`一條出路`,"The plain blocks are walls. A walker stands on square 1 at the back-left and has to reach the exit at the front-right, moving one square at a time.":`普通的方塊是牆。一個行走者站在左後方的 1 號格子上，要一次走一格，到達右前方的出口。`,"It cannot see the maze from above. All it can do is try a direction and find out.":`它沒法從上方俯瞰迷宮。它能做的只是試一個方向，看看結果。`,exit:`出口`,Trail:`足跡`,squares:`格`,"Squares stepped on":`走過的格子`,"Backed out of":`退出來的`,"Pick an order and keep to it":`選一個順序並堅持下去`,"The rule: at every square try <strong>right</strong> first, then forward, then left, then back. Take the first way that is open, and leave a numbered marker on each square.":`規則是：在每個格子上先試<strong>右</strong>，然後前，然後左，然後後。走第一條通的路，並在每個格子上留一個帶編號的標記。`,"Right is open three times running. Then there is a wall ahead and nothing new on any side.":`右邊連續三次都是通的。然後前方是牆，各個方向都沒有新路了。`,"dead end":`死路`,"Back up to the last choice":`退回到上一個選擇`,"Pick up marker 4 and step back. Square 3 has no other way out either, so pick that up too.":`撿起 4 號標記，退一步。3 號格子也沒有別的出路，所以把它也撿起來。`,"Square 2 is different. Right has been tried, but <strong>forward</strong> has not, and it is open.":`2 號格子不一樣。右邊已經試過了，但<strong>前</strong>還沒試，而且是通的。`,"forward is untried":`前還沒試過`,"Carry on from there":`從那裡繼續`,"Forward, and forward again. Now right is open once more, and right is always tried first.":`往前，再往前。現在右邊又通了，而右邊總是先試。`,"The markers are numbered 3, 4, 5: the old 3 and 4 were picked up, so the trail only ever shows the way that is still alive.":`標記的編號是 3、4、5：舊的 3 和 4 被撿起來了，所以足跡只顯示仍然活著的那條路。`,Out:`出去了`,"A wall to the right, so forward. Then right, onto the exit.":`右邊是牆，所以往前。然後往右，走到出口上。`,"The trail left on the floor is the route: seven squares, start to finish. The dead end is not part of it.":`留在地上的足跡就是路線：七個格子，從起點到終點。死路不是它的一部分。`,"The same search everywhere":`到處都是同樣的搜尋`,"The trail is the recursion stack: each marker is one call still waiting for an answer. Picking a marker up is that call returning “no”.":`足跡就是遞迴堆疊：每個標記都是一次仍在等答案的呼叫。撿起一個標記，就是那次呼叫返回了「否」。`,"Sudoku is the same search with digits in place of directions: write one in, carry on, and if a square has no digit left to try, rub out the last one and try the next.":`數獨是同樣的搜尋，只是用數字代替方向：填一個進去，繼續；如果某個格子沒有數字可試了，就擦掉上一個，試下一個。`,"This finds a way out, not the shortest. For the shortest, use breadth-first search.":`這找到的是一條出路，而不是最短的。要最短的，就用廣度優先搜尋。`,"One square, row 2 column 0, was never visited.":`有一個格子，第 2 行第 0 列，從沒被訪問過。`},i={"if n < 2: return n":`如果 n < 2: 返回 n`,"if memo has n: return memo[n]      // seen it before":`如果 memo 裡有 n: 返回 memo[n]      // 以前見過`,"memo[n] ← answer                   // write it down":`memo[n] ← answer                   // 把它記下來`,"return answer":`返回 answer`,"What is remembered":`記住了什麼`,"A recursion that branches":`會分叉的遞迴`,"Each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before it: fib(n) = fib(n − 1) + fib(n − 2). Written as a recursive function, every call makes two more.":`每個斐波那契數都是前兩個數的和：fib(n) = fib(n − 1) + fib(n − 2)。寫成遞迴函式，每次呼叫都會再發起兩次呼叫。`,"Here is every call made to work out fib(4). Each node is one call, labelled with its n. Nine calls, for a very small number.":`這裡是算 fib(4) 時發起的每一次呼叫。每個節點是一次呼叫，標著它的 n。九次呼叫，就為了一個很小的數。`,Memo:`備忘錄`,"The same work, twice":`同樣的工作做了兩遍`,"Look at the two calls for fib(2). They are the same question, and each works out the same answer from scratch, with its own calls below it.":`看看兩次 fib(2) 呼叫。它們是同一個問題，而每次都從頭算出同樣的答案，各自下面還有自己的呼叫。`,"It gets worse quickly. fib(5) repeats the whole of fib(3) twice. fib(40) makes over 300 million calls, nearly all of them repeats.":`情況很快就變得更糟。fib(5) 把整個 fib(3) 重複了兩次。fib(40) 要發起三億多次呼叫，幾乎全是重複。`,"About 1.6 times as many calls for each step up in n: exponential.":`n 每增加 1，呼叫次數大約變成 1.6 倍：指數級。`,"worked out again":`又算了一遍`,"fib(2) is worked out twice, fib(1) three times.":`fib(2) 算了兩次，fib(1) 算了三次。`,"Write the answers down":`把答案記下來`,"The fix is almost embarrassingly simple. The first time a call finishes, save its answer in a table, the <strong>memo</strong>, under its n.":`修正方法簡單得幾乎讓人不好意思。一次呼叫第一次完成時，就把它的答案按 n 存進一張表，也就是<strong>備忘錄</strong>。`,"Follow the left side down and back up: fib(2) is 1, then fib(3) is 2. Both are now written down.":`沿左邊往下走再回來：fib(2) 是 1，然後 fib(3) 是 2。兩個現在都記下來了。`,"Look it up instead":`改為查表`,"Now the right side asks for fib(2) again. Before doing any work, check the memo: the answer is already there.":`現在右邊又要 fib(2)。在做任何工作之前，先查備忘錄：答案已經在那裡了。`,"That call returns at once, and the calls it would have made never happen. A whole subtree is gone.":`那次呼叫立刻返回，它原本會發起的呼叫都不會發生。整棵子樹都沒了。`,"from the memo":`來自備忘錄`,"Each question once":`每個問題只算一次`,"fib(4) is 2 + 1 = 3, from seven calls instead of nine. The saving grows fast: with a memo, fib(40) takes 79 calls, not 300 million.":`fib(4) 是 2 + 1 = 3，用了七次呼叫而不是九次。節省得越來越多：有了備忘錄，fib(40) 只要 79 次呼叫，而不是三億次。`,"This is <strong>dynamic programming</strong>, top-down: ordinary recursion, plus a table so that no subproblem is solved twice.":`這就是自頂向下的<strong>動態規劃</strong>：普通的遞迴，加上一張表，讓任何子問題都不會被解兩次。`,"O(n): there are only n + 1 different questions, and each is answered once.":`O(n)：只有 n + 1 個不同的問題，每個只回答一次。`,"When it works":`什麼時候管用`,Recognise:`識別`,"Memoization pays off when two things are true. The problem breaks into smaller problems of the same kind. And those smaller problems <em>overlap</em>: the same ones come up again and again.":`兩件事都成立時，記憶化才划算。問題能拆成同類的更小問題。並且這些更小的問題會<em>重疊</em>：同樣的問題一再出現。`,"Fibonacci has both. Merge sort has only the first: its halves never repeat, so there is nothing to remember.":`斐波那契兩樣都有。合併排序只有第一樣：它的兩半從不重複，所以沒什麼要記的。`,"A recursion that keeps asking the same questions wants a memo.":`一個不斷問同樣問題的遞迴，需要一個備忘錄。`,"Overlapping subproblems are the sign.":`重疊子問題就是訊號。`},a={"for i from 2 to n:":`對於 i 從 2 到 n:`,"return table[n]":`返回 table[n]`,"The table":`表`,"Start from the bottom":`從底部開始`,"Memoization starts with the big question and works down, saving answers as it goes. <strong>Tabulation</strong> turns that round: answer the smallest questions first, and build up.":`記憶化從大問題開始往下做，邊做邊儲存答案。<strong>製表法</strong>反過來：先回答最小的問題，再一步步往上搭。`,"There is no recursion. There is just a table, with one cell for each subproblem, filled in an order that makes sure everything a cell needs is already there.":`沒有遞迴。只有一張表，每個子問題一個格子，按一定順序填寫，保證每個格子需要的東西都已經在那裡了。`,Additions:`加法次數`,"One cell for each of fib(0) to fib(7).":`fib(0) 到 fib(7) 各一個格子。`,"The base cases":`基本情況`,"Two answers need no working out: fib(0) is 0 and fib(1) is 1. Write them in.":`有兩個答案不需要算：fib(0) 是 0，fib(1) 是 1。把它們填進去。`,"These are the same base cases the recursion had. Here they are simply where the table starts.":`這些就是遞迴裡的那些基本情況。在這裡，它們只是表開始的地方。`,"Each from the two before":`每個都由前兩個得出`,"fib(2) is fib(1) + fib(0). Both are already in the table, so it is one addition: 1.":`fib(2) 是 fib(1) + fib(0)。兩個都已經在表裡了，所以只是一次加法：1。`,"Nothing was called and nothing was looked for. The two cells to its left were simply read.":`沒有呼叫任何東西，也沒有查詢任何東西。只是讀了它左邊的兩個格子。`,"Left to right":`從左到右`,"Carry on along the row. Each new cell reads its two neighbours on the left and adds them: 2, then 3, then 5.":`沿著這一排繼續。每個新格子讀取它左邊的兩個鄰居並相加：2，然後 3，然後 5。`,"The order matters. Going left to right means a cell is never read before it has been written.":`順序很重要。從左到右意味著一個格子永遠不會在被寫入之前被讀取。`,"The answer is the last cell":`答案在最後一個格子`,"Two more and the table is full: fib(7) is 13.":`再填兩個，表就滿了：fib(7) 是 13。`,"Eight cells, six additions. The recursive version, with nothing saved, makes 41 calls to get the same number.":`八個格子，六次加法。不儲存任何東西的遞迴版本，要發起 41 次呼叫才能得到同一個數。`,"O(n) time: one pass along the table, constant work per cell.":`O(n) 時間：沿著表走一趟，每個格子的工作量是常數。`,"Keep only what you need":`只保留需要的`,Refine:`精簡`,"Look at what each cell actually read: only the two before it. Everything further left is never used again.":`看看每個格子實際讀了什麼：只有它前面的兩個。更左邊的一切再也不會被用到。`,"So the whole table can be replaced by two variables. Seeing which cells are still needed is something a table makes easy, and recursion hides.":`所以整張表可以換成兩個變數。哪些格子還需要，用表來看一目瞭然，用遞迴就看不出來。`,"Memo or table?":`備忘錄還是表？`,"Same idea, same speed. The table avoids deep recursion; the memo only solves the subproblems it meets.":`同樣的思路，同樣的速度。表避免了很深的遞迴；備忘錄只解它遇到的子問題。`,"Memory: O(1) instead of O(n).":`記憶體：O(1) 而不是 O(n)。`},o={"for each item i, of weight w and value v:":`對每個 物品 i，重量為 w，價值為 v:`,"for c from 0 to capacity:":`對於 c 從 0 到 capacity:`,"if w ≤ c: take ← v + best[i − 1][c − w]":`如果 w ≤ c: take ← v + best[i − 1][c − w]`,"best[i][c] ← the larger of leave and take":`best[i][c] ← leave 和 take 中較大的`,"return best[last item][capacity]":`返回 best[最後一個物品][capacity]`,"The items":`物品`,"What to pack":`裝什麼`,"A bag holds 5 kg. There are three items, each with a weight and a value, and each can be taken once or left behind. Which choice is worth the most?":`一個包能裝 5 kg。有三個物品，每個都有重量和價值，每個可以拿一次或者不拿。哪種選擇價值最高？`,"Trying every combination doubles with each item. Instead, ask a smaller question many times: <em>the best from the first few items, in a bag of a given size</em>. The table has a cell for each. With no items, the answer is 0 for every size.":`試遍每種組合，每多一個物品就翻一倍。換個辦法，多次問一個更小的問題：<em>只用前幾個物品，在給定大小的包裡能得到的最好結果</em>。表格為每個這樣的問題準備了一個格子。沒有物品時，任何大小的答案都是 0。`,"Item A":`物品 A`,"worth 3":`價值 3`,"Item B":`物品 B`,"worth 4":`價值 4`,"Item C":`物品 C`,"worth 5":`價值 5`,"The bag holds":`包能裝`,"One item":`一個物品`,"Now allow item A: 2 kg, worth 3. In a bag of 0 or 1 kg it does not fit, so the best is still 0.":`現在允許用物品 A：2 kg，價值 3。在 0 或 1 kg 的包裡裝不下，所以最好的仍然是 0。`,"From 2 kg upwards it fits, and taking it is better than nothing: 3 all the way along.":`從 2 kg 開始就裝得下了，拿它總比什麼都沒有好：一路都是 3。`,"A fits: worth 3":`A 裝得下：價值 3`,"Take it or leave it":`拿還是不拿`,"Add item B (3 kg, worth 4), and look at the 5 kg bag. Two choices. <strong>Leave</strong> B: the answer is the cell above, 3. <strong>Take</strong> B: that is 4, plus the best that fits in the 2 kg left over, which the row above already knows: 3.":`加上物品 B（3 kg，價值 4），看看 5 kg 的包。兩個選擇。<strong>不拿</strong> B：答案是上面的格子，3。<strong>拿</strong> B：那是 4，再加上剩下的 2 kg 裡能裝的最好結果，而上一行已經知道了：3。`,"4 + 3 = 7 beats 3. Every cell in the table is filled by this same comparison.":`4 + 3 = 7 勝過 3。表裡的每個格子都是由同樣的比較填出來的。`,"The last row":`最後一行`,"Item C is 4 kg, worth 5. In the 5 kg bag, taking it leaves 1 kg, and the best for 1 kg is 0: so 5 in total. Leaving it keeps the 7 above.":`物品 C 是 4 kg，價值 5。在 5 kg 的包裡，拿它會剩下 1 kg，而 1 kg 最好是 0：所以總共 5。不拿它就保留上面的 7。`,"7 wins. The bottom-right cell is the answer to the whole problem.":`7 勝出。右下角的格子就是整個問題的答案。`,"Each row only ever reads the row above it.":`每一行只會讀取它上面的那一行。`,"Which items, though?":`那麼是哪些物品？`,"The table gives the value. To find the items, walk back from the answer. If a cell equals the one above it, that item was left. If not, it was taken: move up a row and left by its weight.":`表給出的是價值。要找出物品，就從答案往回走。如果一個格子等於它上面的格子，那個物品就沒拿。如果不等，就是拿了：往上移一行，再往左移它的重量那麼多。`,"7 equals the 7 above: C was left. That 7 differs from the 3 above it: B was taken, leaving 2 kg. And 3 differs from 0: A was taken.":`7 等於上面的 7：C 沒拿。那個 7 不同於它上面的 3：B 拿了，剩下 2 kg。而 3 不同於 0：A 拿了。`,"pack A and B":`裝 A 和 B`,"A and B: 5 kg, worth 7.":`A 和 B：5 kg，價值 7。`,"What it cost":`代價是多少`,"Three items and six bag sizes: 24 cells, each one comparison. With 100 items and a 1,000 kg bag it is 100,000 cells, where trying every combination would never finish.":`三個物品，六種包的大小：24 個格子，每個一次比較。有 100 個物品和一個 1,000 kg 的包時，就是 100,000 個格子，而試遍每種組合永遠也做不完。`,"This shape, a table over “how much of the input” and “how much room”, turns up in budgeting, cutting stock, and scheduling.":`這種形狀，一張以「用了多少輸入」和「還有多少空間」為維度的表，在做預算、切割材料和排程中都會出現。`,"O(items × capacity) in time and space; one row of space if only the value is wanted.":`時間和空間都是 O(物品數 × 容量)；如果只要價值，空間只需一行。`},s={"for i from 1 to length of a:":`對於 i 從 1 到 a 的長度:`,"for j from 1 to length of b:":`對於 j 從 1 到 b 的長度:`,"same[i][j] ← the larger of":`same[i][j] ← 以下兩者中較大的`,"same[i − 1][j] and same[i][j − 1]":`same[i − 1][j] 和 same[i][j − 1]`,"return same[last i][last j]":`返回 same[最後的 i][最後的 j]`,"What two sequences share":`兩個序列有什麼共同點`,"How alike are TAN and ANTS? One measure is their <strong>longest common subsequence</strong>: the longest run of letters that appears in both, in the same order, though not necessarily side by side. Here it is AN.":`TAN 和 ANTS 有多像？一種衡量方法是它們的<strong>最長公共子序列</strong>：在兩者中都出現、順序相同但不一定相鄰的最長字母串。這裡是 AN。`,"The table asks the question of every pair of beginnings: a row for each start of TAN, a column for each start of ANTS. Against an empty word, nothing is shared: 0.":`這張表對每一對開頭部分都問這個問題：TAN 的每個開頭部分佔一行，ANTS 的每個開頭部分佔一列。和空詞相比，沒有任何共同點：0。`,"File comparison, spell checking, matching DNA.":`檔案比較、拼寫檢查、DNA 比對。`,"First word":`第一個詞`,"Second word":`第二個詞`,"When the letters match":`字母相同時`,"Row T. Against A and against AN, T matches nothing: 0. Against ANT, the last letters are the same: T and T.":`T 行。和 A、AN 相比，T 什麼都不匹配：0。和 ANT 相比，最後的字母相同：T 和 T。`,"A match extends whatever the two words shared <em>before</em> those letters. That is the cell up and to the left, plus one: 0 + 1.":`一次匹配會延續兩個詞在這些字母<em>之前</em>共有的東西。那就是左上方的格子，再加一：0 + 1。`,"When they differ":`字母不同時`,"Row TA, column A: a match again, so 1. Now the next cell, TA against AN. The last letters, A and N, differ, so one of them is no help.":`TA 行，A 列：又是匹配，所以是 1。現在是下一個格子，TA 對 AN。最後的字母 A 和 N 不同，所以其中一個沒有幫助。`,"Drop one or the other and take the better result: the cell above, or the cell to the left. Here, 1.":`去掉其中一個，取較好的結果：上面的格子，或者左邊的格子。這裡是 1。`,"Fill the table":`填滿這張表`,"Row TAN. Against AN, N matches N, and before those letters the words shared 1: so 2. After that the letters differ, and the 2 is carried along.":`TAN 行。和 AN 相比，N 匹配 N，而在這些字母之前兩個詞共有 1：所以是 2。之後字母不同，2 一直被帶下去。`,"The bottom-right cell covers both whole words. The longest common subsequence has length 2.":`右下角的格子涵蓋兩個完整的詞。最長公共子序列的長度是 2。`,"Read the letters back":`把字母讀回來`,"To recover the letters, walk back from the corner. Where the letters differ, step to whichever neighbour holds the same number. Where they match, that letter is part of the answer: step diagonally.":`要找回這些字母，就從角上往回走。字母不同的地方，走到存著相同數字的那個鄰居。字母相同的地方，這個字母就是答案的一部分：沿對角線走。`,"The walk passes two matches, N and then A. Read in order: AN.":`這條路經過兩次匹配，先是 N，然後是 A。按順序讀：AN。`,"A, then N":`A，然後 N`,"One pattern, many problems":`一個模式，很多問題`,"Twenty cells, each filled by looking at three neighbours. Comparing every subsequence of one word with the other would double with every letter.":`二十個格子，每個都是看三個鄰居填出來的。把一個詞的每個子序列都和另一個詞比較，每多一個字母就要翻倍。`,"Change the rule in the cell and the same table measures other things: the fewest edits to turn one word into another, or the best way to line up two genes.":`改變格子裡的規則，同一張表就能衡量別的東西：把一個詞變成另一個詞最少要改幾次，或者對齊兩個基因的最佳方式。`,"Longest common subsequence: AN.":`最長公共子序列：AN。`},c={"return bit k of set is on":`返回 set 的第 k 位元是否開著`,"switch bit k on":`開啟第 k 位元`,"return a AND b":`返回 a AND b`,"return a OR b":`返回 a OR b`,"return a AND (NOT b)":`返回 a AND (NOT b)`,"The sets":`集合`,"A set in a single number":`一個數裡的集合`,"To store a set of small numbers, give every possible member one bit: on if it is in the set, off if it is not. The cells are numbered 7 down to 0.":`要存一個由小數字組成的集合，就給每個可能的成員一個位元：在集合裡就開著，不在就關著。格子從 7 往下編號到 0。`,"This row is the set {1, 3, 4}. Is 3 in it? Look at bit 3. No hashing, and no searching.":`這一排就是集合 {1, 3, 4}。3 在裡面嗎？看第 3 位元。不用雜湊，也不用搜尋。`,"3 is in the set":`3 在集合裡`,"contains 3?":`包含 3？`,"Add, remove, look up":`新增、刪除、查詢`,"These are the mask operations again. Adding 6 means switching bit 6 on. Removing a member switches its bit off. Asking is testing a bit.":`這些又是遮罩操作。新增 6 就是開啟第 6 位元。刪除一個成員就是關掉它的位元。詢問就是檢查一個位元。`,"Each is O(1), and all eight possible members fit in one byte.":`每個都是 O(1)，而且全部八個可能的成員都放得進一個位元組。`,"add 6":`新增 6`,"A second set":`第二個集合`,"Behind is another set, B = {3, 4, 5}. Combining two sets usually means walking through the members of both.":`後面是另一個集合，B = {3, 4, 5}。合併兩個集合通常意味著把兩者的成員都走一遍。`,"Here each set is just a number, and the two rows line up bit for bit.":`這裡每個集合都只是一個數，兩排一個位元對一個位元地對齊。`,"Intersection is AND":`交集就是 AND`,Combine:`合併`,"Which members are in <em>both</em>? AND the two numbers. A bit survives only where both rows have a block.":`哪些成員在<em>兩個</em>集合裡？把兩個數做 AND。只有兩排都有方塊的地方，那個位元才會保留。`,"1 and 6 drop out, leaving {3, 4}. Every member was handled at once, by one instruction.":`1 和 6 掉出去了，剩下 {3, 4}。每個成員都同時處理了，用的是一條指令。`,"in both":`兩個都有`,"Union is OR":`並集就是 OR`,"Put A back as it was. Which members are in <em>either</em> set? OR the two numbers: a bit is on if it is on in A or in B.":`把 A 恢復原樣。哪些成員在<em>任意一個</em>集合裡？把兩個數做 OR：在 A 或 B 中開著的位元就是開著的。`,"5 arrives from B, giving {1, 3, 4, 5, 6}. Taking B’s members <em>out</em> of A is A AND (NOT B).":`5 從 B 來，得到 {1, 3, 4, 5, 6}。把 B 的成員<em>從</em> A 中去掉就是 A AND (NOT B)。`,"When the members are small numbers":`當成員是小數字時`,"A real bitset is an array of 64-bit words. A set over a million possible members is about 16,000 words, and a union is 16,000 ORs.":`真正的位元集合是一個由 64 位元字組成的陣列。一個有一百萬個可能成員的集合大約是 16,000 個字，一次並集就是 16,000 次 OR。`,"It only works when members are small whole numbers, or can be numbered. A Bloom filter is built on one; so are the “visited” marks of a graph search and the sieve for finding primes.":`只有當成員是小的整數，或者能被編號時，它才管用。布隆過濾器就是建立在它上面的；圖搜尋中的「已訪問」標記和找素數的篩法也是。`,"O(1) per member. O(n ÷ 64) to combine two whole sets of n possible members.":`每個成員 O(1)。合併兩個有 n 個可能成員的完整集合要 O(n ÷ 64)。`},l={"binary-search":{"A sorted shelf":`排好序的架子`,"Nine numbers, in order from smallest to largest. We want to know where <strong>34</strong> is.":`九個數，從小到大排列。我們想知道 <strong>34</strong> 在哪裡。`,"Checking every block from the left would get there in the end. Because the shelf is sorted, we can do far better.":`從左邊逐個檢查每個方塊，最終也能找到。但因為架子是排好序的，我們可以做得好得多。`,"Binary search only works when the data is sorted.":`二分搜尋只適用於排好序的資料。`,"Look in the middle":`看中間`,"Mark the whole shelf as the search window, from <strong>low</strong> to <strong>high</strong>, and hold 34 up against the block in the middle.":`把整個架子標為搜尋視窗，從 <strong>low</strong> 到 <strong>high</strong>，拿 34 和中間的方塊比一比。`,"It is 28. That is less than 34.":`它是 28。比 34 小。`,"On a sorted shelf, everything to the left of 28 is smaller still. 34 cannot be there.":`在排好序的架子上，28 左邊的一切都更小。34 不可能在那裡。`,"Throw away half":`扔掉一半`,"28 and everything to its left is ruled out in one go. Move <strong>low</strong> to just past the middle.":`28 和它左邊的一切一下子全被排除了。把 <strong>low</strong> 移到中間的後一位。`,"The window is now four blocks wide.":`視窗現在只有四個方塊寬。`,"One look removed five candidates. Checking one by one, it would have removed one.":`看一次就排除了五個候選。逐個檢查的話，只能排除一個。`,"Middle again":`再看中間`,"Do exactly the same thing on what is left. The middle of the window is now 42.":`對剩下的部分做完全相同的事。視窗的中間現在是 42。`,"That is more than 34, so 42 and everything to its right is too big.":`它比 34 大，所以 42 和它右邊的一切都太大了。`,"That hop was half as long as the first. The next will be half as long again.":`這一跳是第一跳的一半長。下一跳又會是一半長。`,"And the other side":`再看另一邊`,"Move <strong>high</strong> to just before the middle. Low and high now point at the same block.":`把 <strong>high</strong> 移到中間的前一位。low 和 high 現在指向同一個方塊。`,"One candidate is left.":`只剩一個候選了。`,"Hold it up one last time: <strong>34 = 34</strong>. Found at index 5, after three looks.":`最後再比一次：<strong>34 = 34</strong>。在索引 5 找到，看了三次。`,"Had it been some other number, the window would have closed with nothing in it, and we would know 34 is not on the shelf.":`如果是別的數，視窗就會在裡面什麼都沒有時合上，我們就知道 34 不在架子上。`,"Going one by one from the left would have taken six looks.":`從左邊逐個看的話，要看六次。`,"Every look halves the window. So the number of looks depends on how many times you can halve n before one block is left: <strong>O(log n)</strong>.":`每看一次，視窗就減半。所以要看的次數取決於 n 能減半多少次才剩下一個方塊：<strong>O(log n)</strong>。`,"Double the length of the shelf and the search needs just one more look.":`架子長度翻倍，搜尋只需多看一次。`,"A million sorted items never take more than 20 looks.":`一百萬個排好序的項，永遠不會超過 20 次。`},"binary-search-on-answer":{"while lo < hi:":`當 lo < hi:`,"mid ← halfway between lo and hi":`mid ← lo 和 hi 的中點`,"if works(mid):":`如果 works(mid):`,"hi ← mid          // mid may be the answer":`hi ← mid          // mid 可能就是答案`,"lo ← mid + 1      // mid is too small":`lo ← mid + 1      // mid 太小了`,"return lo":`返回 lo`,"load the parcels in order, starting a new":`按順序裝包裹，下一個裝不下時`,"trip when the next one will not fit":`就開始新的一趟`,"return trips used ≤ trips allowed":`返回 用掉的趟數 ≤ 允許的趟數`,"No array to search":`沒有陣列可搜`,"Three parcels weighing 5, 3 and 4 must go out in order, in at most two trips. What is the <strong>smallest lorry</strong> that can do it?":`重 5、3、4 的三個包裹必須按順序送出，最多送兩趟。能做到的<strong>最小卡車</strong>是多大？`,"It must hold the biggest parcel, so at least 5. A lorry of 12 takes everything at once. The answer is somewhere in the row 5 to 12, and nothing in the problem is sorted.":`它必須裝得下最大的包裹，所以至少是 5。容量 12 的卡車一次就能裝下全部。答案在 5 到 12 這一排裡的某處，而問題裡沒有任何東西是排好序的。`,Parcels:`包裹`,"in this order":`按這個順序`,"Trips allowed":`允許的趟數`,"Could still be":`仍有可能`,"5 to 12":`5 到 12`,"Sizes tested":`已測試的容量`,"Guess the middle and check":`猜中間，然後檢查`,"Finding the best size directly is awkward. <em>Checking</em> one size is easy: load parcels until the next will not fit, then start a new trip.":`直接找出最佳容量很麻煩。<em>檢查</em>一個容量卻很容易：裝包裹，直到下一個裝不下，然後開始新的一趟。`,"Try 8. First trip 5 + 3, second trip 4. Two trips: it works. So anything bigger works too, and hi comes down to 8.":`試試 8。第一趟 5 + 3，第二趟 4。兩趟：可行。所以更大的也都可行，hi 降到 8。`,"5+3, then 4":`5+3，然後 4`,"5 to 8":`5 到 8`,"Too small":`太小`,"Middle of 5 to 8: try 6. Trip one takes 5, trip two takes 3, and 4 is left over. Three trips: it fails.":`5 到 8 的中間：試試 6。第一趟裝 5，第二趟裝 3，4 剩下了。三趟：不行。`,"So anything smaller fails too. lo moves past it, to 7.":`所以更小的也都不行。lo 越過它，移到 7。`,"5, 3, 4: three trips":`5、3、4：三趟`,"7 to 8":`7 到 8`,"Closing in":`逼近`,"Try 7. Trip one takes 5, trip two takes 3 + 4. It works, so hi comes down to 7.":`試試 7。第一趟裝 5，第二趟裝 3 + 4。可行，所以 hi 降到 7。`,"lo and hi now meet. The smallest lorry is 7, found with three checks.":`lo 和 hi 現在相遇了。最小的卡車是 7，檢查了三次就找到了。`,"5, then 3+4":`5，然後 3+4`,"The sorted row was hidden":`排好序的一排藏起來了`,"Why it works":`為什麼可行`,"Write down the answer to “does this size work?” for every size, and the row reads no, no, yes, yes, yes… All the noes come first, then all the yeses.":`把每個容量對「這個容量可行嗎？」的回答寫下來，這一排讀起來就是否、否、是、是、是……所有的「否」在前，然後全是「是」。`,"That is a sorted row. Binary search needs nothing more: it is looking for the place where no turns into yes.":`這就是一排排好序的東西。二分搜尋不需要別的：它要找的就是「否」變成「是」的那個位置。`,"Never worked out: 5, 9, 10, 11, 12.":`從沒算過：5、9、10、11、12。`,"Smallest that works":`最小的可行值`,"Look for this shape: “the smallest X such that…” or “the largest X such that…”, where a check is easy and making X bigger can only help.":`留意這種形式：「滿足……的最小 X」或者「滿足……的最大 X」，其中檢查很容易，而且讓 X 變大隻會有幫助。`,"The slowest speed that still arrives on time. The largest gap you can keep between items. The smallest page size that fits a book into k volumes.":`仍能準時到達的最慢速度。物品之間能保持的最大間距。能把一本書裝進 k 卷的最小頁面大小。`,"O(n) per check, and log(range) checks: O(n log range) in all.":`每次檢查 O(n)，檢查 log(範圍) 次：總共 O(n log 範圍)。`},"simple-sorts":{"find the smallest item from i onwards":`找出從 i 開始往後最小的項`,"swap it into cell i":`把它交換到格子 i`,"for each item, from the second onwards:":`對每個 項，從第二個開始:`,"lift it out":`把它拿出來`,"shift every bigger item before it one cell right":`把它前面每個更大的項右移一格`,"put it down in the gap":`把它放進空出來的位置`,"Put them in order":`把它們排好序`,"Six numbers, in no order. Sorting is one of the oldest problems in computing, and a sorted array is what makes binary search possible.":`六個數，沒有順序。排序是計算機領域最古老的問題之一，而排好序的陣列正是二分搜尋的前提。`,"The simple sorts all work the same way: grow a sorted part at one end, one item at a time. They are easy to write and easy to trust.":`簡單排序的原理都一樣：在一端擴充套件一個已排序的部分，一次一項。它們容易寫，也容易讓人放心。`,Method:`方法`,"In order so far":`目前已就位`,"Selection: find the smallest":`選擇：找出最小的`,"Selection sort":`選擇排序`,"Look at every item and remember the smallest seen so far: 5, then 2, then 1. Swap it into the first cell.":`看每一項，記住目前見過最小的：5，然後 2，然後 1。把它交換到第一個格子。`,"Cell 0 now holds the right value for good. It is never looked at again.":`格子 0 現在永久存著正確的值。再也不會看它了。`,"Then the next smallest":`然後是第二小的`,"Do the same with what is left. The smallest of the rest is 2, already in place. After it comes 3, which swaps with 8.":`對剩下的做同樣的事。其餘中最小的是 2，已經就位了。之後是 3，它和 8 交換。`,"Each pass scans everything that is not yet sorted, and fixes exactly one more cell.":`每一趟都掃描所有還沒排好的項，並且恰好多確定一個格子。`,"2: already in place":`2：已經就位`,"Until nothing is left":`直到什麼都不剩`,"Two more swaps and the row is sorted.":`再交換兩次，這一排就排好了。`,"Six items took six passes, and each pass looked at everything unsorted: 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 comparisons. Double the items and that is four times the work.":`六個項用了六趟，每趟都要看所有沒排好的：5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 次比較。項數翻倍，工作量就變成四倍。`,"O(n²) comparisons, always. At most n swaps, which is the one thing it is good at.":`比較次數總是 O(n²)。交換最多 n 次，這是它唯一擅長的地方。`,"15 comparisons for 6 items.":`6 個項比較 15 次。`,"Insertion: a sorted part":`插入：一個已排序的部分`,"Insertion sort":`插入排序`,"Start again with the same six, and a different idea. Treat the first item as a sorted list of one.":`用同樣的六個數重新開始，換一個思路。把第一項當作只有一項的有序列表。`,"Then take the items one at a time and slot each into its place in that list. It is how most people sort a hand of cards.":`然後一次取一項，把每一項插到那個列表中它該在的位置。大多數人整理手裡的撲克牌就是這樣做的。`,"sorted, so far":`目前已排序`,"Lift, shift, drop":`拿起、挪動、放下`,"Take 2. It is smaller than 5, so lift it out, slide 5 one cell to the right, and put 2 down in the gap.":`取 2。它比 5 小，所以把它拿出來，把 5 右移一格，再把 2 放進空位。`,"The sorted part is now two long.":`已排序的部分現在有兩項長。`,"Only as far as needed":`只走需要走的距離`,"8 is already bigger than everything before it: one comparison, no moves. 3 has to go back past 8 and 5, and stops when it meets 2.":`8 已經比它前面的一切都大：一次比較，不用移動。3 要退過 8 和 5，遇到 2 時停下。`,"An item only travels as far as it is out of place.":`一項只會移動它偏離位置的那麼遠。`,"8 > 5: stays":`8 > 5：不動`,"Simple, and sometimes right":`簡單，有時正合適`,"1 travels all the way to the front; 6 moves back one place. Sorted.":`1 一路走到最前面；6 往回挪一位。排好了。`,"In the worst case insertion sort is O(n²) too. But on data that is already nearly sorted it does almost nothing, close to O(n), which is why real sorting libraries use it for small or nearly sorted pieces.":`最壞情況下插入排序也是 O(n²)。但在已經差不多排好的資料上，它幾乎什麼都不用做，接近 O(n)，所以真正的排序庫會用它來處理小的或幾乎有序的片段。`,Also:`另外`,"Bubble sort, which swaps neighbours that are out of order, is the third simple sort. It is O(n²) and rarely the best choice.":`氣泡排序交換順序不對的相鄰項，是第三種簡單排序。它是 O(n²)，很少是最好的選擇。`},"merge-sort":{"if a has fewer than two items: return a":`如果 a 少於兩項: 返回 a`,"left ← merge_sort(the first half)":`left ← merge_sort(前一半)`,"right ← merge_sort(the second half)":`right ← merge_sort(後一半)`,"return merge(left, right)":`返回 merge(left, right)`,"while both have items:":`當 兩邊都還有項:`,"move the smaller of their front items to the output":`把兩邊隊首中較小的移到輸出`,"move whatever is left over to the output":`把剩下的全部移到輸出`,"Divide and conquer":`分治`,"The simple sorts take about n² steps. <strong>Merge sort</strong> does much better, with an idea borrowed from recursion: a big sorting problem is two smaller sorting problems.":`簡單排序大約要 n² 步。<strong>合併排序</strong>做得好得多，它借用了遞迴的思路：一個大的排序問題就是兩個小的排序問題。`,"Sort the left half. Sort the right half. Then combine two sorted halves into one, which turns out to be easy.":`排好左半邊。排好右半邊。然後把兩個排好的半邊合成一個，而這件事其實很容易。`,"Moved to the output":`已移到輸出`,"Levels of halving":`對半分的層數`,"Moves per level":`每層移動次數`,"Split in half":`對半分`,"Cut the row down the middle. Nothing is compared and nothing moves: the split is just two index ranges.":`從中間切開這一排。不做比較，也不移動任何東西：切分只是兩個索引範圍。`,"Each half is a smaller copy of the original problem.":`每一半都是原問題的一個更小的副本。`,"Sort each half the same way":`用同樣的方法排好每一半`,"Each half is sorted by merge sort itself: split again, and again, until the pieces are one item long. A single item is already sorted. That is the base case.":`每一半都由合併排序自己來排：再切，再切，直到每塊只有一項長。單獨一項本來就是有序的。這就是基本情況。`,"Trust the recursion for now. What comes back is two sorted halves: 2 3 5 8 and 1 4 6 7.":`現在先相信遞迴。返回來的是兩個排好的半邊：2 3 5 8 和 1 4 6 7。`,"Each half is in order. The whole row is not.":`每一半都是有序的。整排還不是。`,"Merge: compare the fronts":`合併：比較隊首`,Merge:`合併`,"Now the real work. The smallest item overall must be at the front of one half or the other, so compare just those two: 1 beats 2. Move it to the output.":`現在是真正的工作。所有項中最小的一定在某一半的最前面，所以只比較這兩個：1 勝過 2。把它移到輸出。`,"Again: 2 against 4. Each move takes one comparison.":`再來：2 對 4。每次移動只要一次比較。`,"Keep taking the smaller":`一直取較小的`,"3, then 4, then 5, 6 and 7. Every time, only the two front items are looked at, because each half is already in order.":`3，然後 4，然後 5、6 和 7。每次只看兩個隊首的項，因為每一半都已經有序。`,"The second half has run out.":`後一半用完了。`,"With one half empty, whatever is left in the other goes straight across. Eight items merged with eight moves.":`一半空了之後，另一半剩下的直接移過去。八個項，八次移動就合併好了。`,"Every level of splitting needs one such pass over all n items, and halving 8 down to 1 takes 3 levels: log₂ n of them. So the whole sort is n × log n, on any input.":`每一層切分都需要對全部 n 個項過一遍，而把 8 對半分到 1 要 3 層：log₂ n 層。所以整個排序是 n × log n，對任何輸入都是。`,"O(n log n) always. The price is the second row: O(n) extra space.":`總是 O(n log n)。代價是第二排：O(n) 額外空間。`,"For a million items: 20 levels, not a million passes.":`一百萬個項：20 層，而不是一百萬趟。`},"quick-sort":{"if a has fewer than two items: return":`如果 a 少於兩項: 返回`,"quick_sort(everything before p)":`quick_sort(p 之前的一切)`,"quick_sort(everything after p)":`quick_sort(p 之後的一切)`,"pivot ← the last item":`pivot ← 最後一項`,"i ← the first cell":`i ← 第一個格子`,"for each item before the pivot, at j:":`對每個 基準之前的項，位置為 j:`,"if it is smaller than the pivot:":`如果 它比基準小:`,"swap it into cell i, and move i along":`把它交換到格子 i，然後 i 前移`,"swap the pivot into cell i":`把基準交換到格子 i`,"return i":`返回 i`,"Around the pivot":`圍繞基準`,"Pick a pivot":`選一個基準`,"Merge sort splits blindly and does its work when combining. <strong>Quick sort</strong> does the work first: it splits <em>by value</em>, so that no combining is needed.":`合併排序盲目地切分，在合併時才幹活。<strong>快速排序</strong>先幹活：它<em>按值</em>切分，這樣就不需要合併了。`,"Choose one item as the <strong>pivot</strong>, here the last, 4. The aim is to get everything smaller to its left and everything bigger to its right.":`選一項作為<strong>基準</strong>，這裡選最後一項 4。目標是讓所有更小的都在它左邊，所有更大的都在它右邊。`,"the pivot":`基準`,Pivot:`基準`,"Smaller, on its left":`更小的，在它左邊`,"Bigger, on its right":`更大的，在它右邊`,"Smaller ones go left":`小的去左邊`,Partition:`劃分`,"Scan along with j. Cell i marks where the next small item should go. 5 is bigger than the pivot: leave it. 2 is smaller: swap it into cell i, and move i along.":`用 j 往後掃。格子 i 標記下一個小項該放的位置。5 比基準大：不動。2 更小：把它交換到格子 i，然後 i 前移。`,"5 > 4: leave it":`5 > 4：不動`,"2 < 4: goes left":`2 < 4：去左邊`,"Keep scanning":`繼續掃描`,"8 stays. 3 is small: swap it into cell i. 7 stays. 1 is small: swap. 6 stays.":`8 不動。3 小：把它交換到格子 i。7 不動。1 小：交換。6 不動。`,"Everything before i is now smaller than the pivot, and everything from i up to the pivot is bigger. Neither side is sorted, and that is fine.":`現在 i 之前的一切都比基準小，從 i 到基準之間的一切都更大。兩邊都沒排序，這沒關係。`,"The pivot drops into place":`基準落到位`,"Finally swap the pivot into cell i, between the two groups.":`最後把基準交換到格子 i，放在兩組之間。`,"4 is now exactly where it will be in the sorted row: three smaller items before it, four bigger after. It never moves again.":`4 現在正好在它在有序排列中的位置：前面三個更小的項，後面四個更大的。它再也不會移動了。`,"The same again, each side":`兩邊各做一遍同樣的事`,"Now sort the left group and the right group in the same way: pick a pivot, partition, repeat. Each partition puts one more item in its final place and leaves two smaller problems.":`現在用同樣的方法排左邊一組和右邊一組：選基準、劃分、重複。每次劃分都讓多一個項到達最終位置，並留下兩個更小的問題。`,"When the pieces are down to one item, the whole row is sorted. Nothing has to be merged.":`當每塊只剩一項時，整排就排好了。不需要合併任何東西。`,"Fast, usually":`通常很快`,"When the pivot lands near the middle, the row halves each time: log n levels of n work, like merge sort, but in place and with less copying. In practice it is often the fastest sort there is.":`當基準落在中間附近時，這一排每次都會減半：log n 層，每層 n 的工作，和合併排序一樣，但它是原地進行的，複製也更少。實踐中它往往是最快的排序。`,"When the pivot is always the smallest or biggest, one side is empty and nothing halves. On a row that is already sorted, “pick the last item” does exactly that.":`如果基準總是最小或最大的，一邊就是空的，什麼都沒減半。在已經排好序的一排上，「選最後一項」恰好就會這樣。`,"O(n log n) on average, O(n²) at worst. Picking the pivot at random makes the worst case vanishingly unlikely.":`平均 O(n log n)，最壞 O(n²)。隨機選基準能讓最壞情況幾乎不可能出現。`,"sorted in place":`原地排好`,"No second row was needed.":`不需要第二排。`},quickselect:e,"counting-radix-sort":{"for each item x in a:":`對每個 a 中的項 x:`,"put x in bucket x":`把 x 放進 x 號桶`,"read the buckets back in order":`按順序把桶裡的東西讀回來`,"for each digit, from the last to the first:":`對每個 數位，從最後一位到第一位:`,"put each item in the bucket for that digit,":`把每一項放進對應這個數位的桶，`,"keeping the order they arrive in":`保持它們到達的順序`,"Sorting without comparing":`不用比較的排序`,"Every sort so far works by comparing two items, and no such sort can beat n log n. But comparing is not the only way.":`到目前為止的每種排序都是靠比較兩項來工作的，而這樣的排序都不可能快過 n log n。但比較並不是唯一的方法。`,"If the items are small whole numbers, a number can be used as an <em>address</em>. Behind the row is a bucket for each possible value, 0 to 5.":`如果這些項是小的整數，數字本身就可以當作<em>地址</em>用。這一排後面，每個可能的值都有一個桶，從 0 到 5。`,Comparisons:`比較次數`,Moves:`移動次數`,"Each to its own bucket":`各進各的桶`,"Counting sort":`計數排序`,"Take the items in order and drop each into the bucket with its number. 3 goes to bucket 3, 1 to bucket 1.":`按順序取出每一項，把它丟進和它數字相同的桶。3 進 3 號桶，1 進 1 號桶。`,"No item is ever compared with another. Each one knows where it belongs.":`沒有任何一項和別的項比較過。每一項都知道自己該去哪裡。`,"Read the buckets back":`把桶讀回來`,"Now empty the buckets from left to right. The values come out in order, because the buckets <em>are</em> in order.":`現在從左到右清空各個桶。值按順序出來了，因為這些桶<em>本身</em>就是有序的。`,"Two passes, and the work depends on the number of items plus the number of buckets, not on n log n.":`兩趟，而工作量取決於項數加上桶數，而不是 n log n。`,"O(n + k) for n items and k possible values. Only sensible when k is small.":`n 個項、k 種可能的值時為 O(n + k)。只有 k 很小時才合理。`,"Bigger numbers":`更大的數`,"Radix sort":`基數排序`,"These numbers go up to 51. One bucket per possible value would mean dozens of buckets, mostly empty, and for bigger numbers, millions.":`這些數最大到 51。每個可能的值一個桶，就意味著要幾十個桶，大部分是空的；數再大一些，就要幾百萬個。`,"<strong>Radix sort</strong> keeps the six buckets and sorts by one digit at a time instead.":`<strong>基數排序</strong>保留這六個桶，改為一次按一個數位排序。`,"By the last digit":`按最後一位`,"First pass: ignore the tens and bucket each number by its <em>last</em> digit. 32 goes to bucket 2, 15 to bucket 5.":`第一趟：忽略十位，按每個數的<em>最後一位</em>放進桶裡。32 進 2 號桶，15 進 5 號桶。`,"Where two share a bucket, the one that arrived first stays in front: 32 ahead of 12.":`兩個數在同一個桶裡時，先到的留在前面：32 在 12 前面。`,"Read them back":`讀回來`,"Empty the buckets in order, front of each bucket first. The row is now sorted by last digit: 1, 2, 2, 3, 5, 5.":`按順序清空各個桶，每個桶先取前面的。這一排現在按最後一位排好了：1、2、2、3、5、5。`,"It does not look sorted yet. One more pass.":`看起來還沒排好。再來一趟。`,"Then by the first digit":`然後按第一位`,"Second pass: bucket by the tens digit. 12 and 15 both go to bucket 1, and 12 arrives first because the last pass put it first.":`第二趟：按十位放進桶裡。12 和 15 都進 1 號桶，12 先到，因為上一趟把它排在了前面。`,"That is the trick. Keeping arrival order means the work of the earlier pass is not undone.":`訣竅就在這裡。保持到達順序，意味著前一趟的工作不會被打亂。`,"The word for it":`這個性質的名字`,"A sort that keeps equal items in their original order is called stable. Radix sort depends on it.":`讓相等的項保持原來順序的排序叫作穩定排序。基數排序依賴於它。`,"Sorted, digit by digit":`一位一位地排好`,"Read the buckets back once more: 12, 15, 23, 32, 35, 51. Sorted, with not one comparison between two numbers.":`再把桶讀回來一次：12、15、23、32、35、51。排好了，兩個數之間一次比較都沒有。`,"Each pass is a counting sort on one digit, so the total is the number of digits times the size of the input.":`每一趟都是對一個數位的計數排序，所以總量是數位個數乘以輸入的大小。`,"O(d × (n + k)) for d digits. Excellent for fixed-size keys such as integers, dates and postcodes.":`d 個數位時為 O(d × (n + k))。非常適合固定長度的鍵，比如整數、日期和郵政編碼。`,"Two digits: two passes.":`兩個數位：兩趟。`},"stability-and-limits":{"When two keys are equal":`當兩個鍵相等時`,"Two of these cards carry a 3. They are different cards, 3a and 3b, and 3a came first.":`這些卡片中有兩張是 3。它們是不同的卡片，3a 和 3b，而 3a 在前。`,"A sort only cares about the number. So after sorting, which 3 should be in front? There are two honest answers, and sorts differ in which one they give.":`排序只關心數字。那麼排序之後，哪個 3 應該在前面？有兩個說得通的答案，而不同的排序給出的答案不同。`,"3a came first":`3a 在前`,"Sorted with":`使用的排序`,"The two 3s":`兩個 3`,"3a, then 3b":`3a，然後 3b`,Stable:`穩定`,merge:`合併`,counting:`計數`,radix:`基數`,"Not stable":`不穩定`,quick:`快速`,heap:`堆積`,"A long swap jumps the queue":`一次遠距離交換插了隊`,Unstable:`不穩定`,"Selection sort: find the smallest and swap it to the front. 1 swaps with 3a. Then the next smallest, 2, swaps with 3a again.":`選擇排序：找出最小的，把它交換到最前面。1 和 3a 交換。然後第二小的 2 又和 3a 交換。`,"That second swap carried 3a right over 3b. The row is sorted, but the two 3s have changed places. A sort that can do this is <strong>unstable</strong>.":`第二次交換把 3a 直接帶過了 3b。這一排排好了，但兩個 3 換了位置。會這樣做的排序是<strong>不穩定</strong>的。`,"smallest: 1":`最小：1`,"next smallest: 2":`第二小：2`,"3b is now in front":`3b 現在在前面`,"selection sort":`選擇排序`,swapped:`已交換`,"Why anyone minds":`為什麼有人在意`,Why:`為什麼`,"Deal the same four again. Suppose the letter is a name and the number a grade, and the list arrives in name order. Sort it by grade with an unstable sort and the names inside each grade come out shuffled.":`再發同樣的四張。假設字母是名字，數字是成績，列表按名字順序到來。用不穩定的排序按成績排，每個成績裡的名字就會被打亂。`,"A <strong>stable</strong> sort keeps equal keys in the order they arrived. That is what makes “sort by name, then by grade” work.":`<strong>穩定</strong>的排序讓相等的鍵保持它們到達的順序。正是這一點讓「先按名字排，再按成績排」行得通。`,"Insertion never passes an equal":`插入排序從不越過相等的項`,"Insertion sort lifts each card and slides the <em>bigger</em> ones along to make room. 1 goes in front of 3a. 3b is not smaller than 3a, so it stays put.":`插入排序拿起每張卡片，把<em>更大</em>的往後挪來騰出位置。1 放到 3a 前面。3b 不比 3a 小，所以它不動。`,"2 slides in under both 3s, which each move one place and keep their order. Nothing ever hops over a card equal to it.":`2 滑到兩個 3 的前面，兩個 3 各挪一位，保持它們的順序。從來沒有卡片越過和它相等的卡片。`,"3b: not smaller, stays":`3b：不更小，不動`,"still 3a, then 3b":`仍是 3a，然後 3b`,"insertion sort":`插入排序`,"Which sorts are which":`哪些排序是哪種`,Summary:`總結`,"Sorts that only move cards past strictly bigger neighbours, or that merge taking from the left side first, are stable: insertion, merge, counting and radix.":`只讓卡片越過嚴格更大的鄰居的排序，或者合併時先從左邊取的排序，是穩定的：插入、合併、計數和基數。`,"Sorts that swap across a distance are not: selection, quick sort and heap sort. Any of them can be made stable by sorting on the pair (key, original position), at the cost of extra memory.":`遠距離交換的排序不是：選擇排序、快速排序和堆積排序。它們都可以透過按 (鍵, 原始位置) 這一對來排序而變得穩定，代價是額外的記憶體。`,"Radix sort relies on it: each pass must not undo the last.":`基數排序依賴於它：每一趟都不能打亂上一趟。`,"How fast can sorting be?":`排序最快能有多快？`,"A different question about the same cards. A sort that works by comparing learns one thing per comparison: yes or no. Four cards can arrive in 24 different orders, and the sort has to find out which.":`關於同樣這些卡片的另一個問題。靠比較工作的排序，每次比較只能得知一件事：是或否。四張卡片可能有 24 種不同的到達順序，而排序必須找出是哪一種。`,"A yes-or-no answer can at best rule out half of the orders still possible. 24, 12, 6, 3, 2, 1: no method can be sure in fewer than five comparisons.":`一個是或否的回答，最多隻能排除仍然可能的順序中的一半。24、12、6、3、2、1：沒有任何方法能用少於五次比較就確定。`,"one of 24 orders":`24 種順序之一`,"Possible orders of 4 cards":`4 張卡片可能的順序`,"Left after each answer":`每次回答後剩下的`,"at best":`最好情況`,"Comparisons needed":`需要的比較次數`,"at least":`至少`,"For n items":`n 個項時`,"about n log n":`大約 n log n`,"n log n is the floor":`n log n 是下限`,"For n items there are n! orders, and halving that down to one takes about n log n answers. So every comparison sort needs that many in its worst case. Merge sort and heap sort already achieve it: they cannot be beaten, only matched.":`n 個項有 n! 種順序，把它減半到只剩一種大約需要 n log n 個回答。所以每種比較排序在最壞情況下都需要這麼多次。合併排序和堆積排序已經做到了：它們不可能被超越，只能被追平。`,"Counting and radix sort go faster only because they never compare. They read the keys directly, which is a different game with its own conditions.":`計數排序和基數排序之所以更快，只是因為它們從不比較。它們直接讀取鍵，這是另一種玩法，有它自己的條件。`,"The limit":`極限`,"No comparison sort can do better than O(n log n) in the worst case.":`在最壞情況下，沒有比較排序能好過 O(n log n)。`,"Proved, not just observed.":`是證明出來的，不只是觀察到的。`},"interval-scheduling":{"sort them by when they finish":`按結束時間排序`,"free_from ← the start of the day":`free_from ← 一天的開始`,"for each request, in that order:":`對每個 請求，按那個順序:`,"if it starts at or after free_from:":`如果 它在 free_from 或之後開始:`,"take it":`接受它`,"free_from ← when it finishes":`free_from ← 它結束的時間`,"The room":`會議室`,"One room, five requests":`一間會議室，五個請求`,"Five meetings want the same room. Each row is one request, and each block is an hour it needs. Two meetings cannot overlap.":`五個會議想用同一間會議室。每一行是一個請求，每個方塊是它需要的一個小時。兩個會議不能重疊。`,"Which ones should be accepted to fit in <strong>as many meetings as possible</strong>?":`應該接受哪些，才能安排<strong>儘可能多的會議</strong>？`,Taken:`已接受`,"Turned down":`已拒絕`,"Room free from":`會議室空出的時間`,"hour 0":`第 0 小時`,"A rule that sounds right":`聽起來對的規則`,"Wrong turn":`走錯路`,"A <strong>greedy</strong> algorithm makes one simple choice after another and never takes one back. The whole question is which rule to choose by.":`<strong>貪婪</strong>演算法一個接一個地做簡單的選擇，並且從不反悔。整個問題就在於按什麼規則來選。`,"Try “whichever starts first”. That is D, and D holds the room for six hours. Every other request overlaps it: one meeting.":`試試「最先開始的」。那是 D，而 D 佔用會議室六個小時。其他每個請求都和它重疊：一個會議。`,"starts first, blocks four":`最先開始，擋住了四個`,"hour 6":`第 6 小時`,"Whichever finishes first":`最先結束的`,"The rule that works: take the meeting that <strong>finishes earliest</strong>. It hands the room back soonest, leaving the most time for everything else.":`行得通的規則是：選<strong>最早結束</strong>的會議。它最快把會議室交還出來，給其他一切留下最多的時間。`,"The rows are already in that order. A finishes first, at hour 3. Take it.":`各行已經按這個順序排好了。A 最先結束，在第 3 小時。接受它。`,"finishes first":`最先結束`,"hour 3":`第 3 小時`,"Skip what overlaps":`跳過重疊的`,"Go down the list. B starts at hour 2, while A still has the room. Turn it down.":`沿著列表往下走。B 在第 2 小時開始，這時 A 還佔著會議室。拒絕它。`,"C starts at hour 3, exactly as A leaves. Take it. The room is now busy until hour 5.":`C 在第 3 小時開始，正好是 A 離開的時候。接受它。會議室現在一直忙到第 5 小時。`,"starts as A ends":`在 A 結束時開始`,"hour 5":`第 5 小時`,"One pass to the end":`一趟到底`,"D started back at hour 0: turned down. E starts at hour 5, as C leaves: taken.":`D 早在第 0 小時就開始了：拒絕。E 在第 5 小時開始，正好 C 離開：接受。`,"Three meetings, A, C and E, and each request was looked at once.":`三個會議，A、C 和 E，每個請求只看了一次。`,"starts as C ends":`在 C 結束時開始`,"hour 8":`第 8 小時`,"Why it cannot be beaten":`為什麼無法被超越`,"Take any best possible schedule and look at its first meeting. Swap it for A. A finishes no later, so nothing after it is disturbed, and the schedule is just as long.":`取任意一個最佳安排，看它的第一個會議。把它換成 A。A 不會結束得更晚，所以它後面的一切都不受影響，安排也一樣長。`,"So there is always a best schedule that starts with the greedy choice. The same argument then applies to whatever comes after A.":`所以總存在一個以貪婪選擇開頭的最佳安排。同樣的論證也適用於 A 之後的一切。`,"O(n log n) to sort, then one pass.":`排序 O(n log n)，然後一趟。`,"No schedule fits in four.":`沒有任何安排能放下四個。`},"huffman-coding":{"put every letter in a min-heap, by count":`把每個字母按次數放進一個最小堆積`,"while the heap holds more than one node:":`當 堆積中不止一個節點:`,"a ← pop the smallest":`a ← 彈出最小的`,"b ← pop the smallest":`b ← 彈出最小的`,"push a new node worth a + b,":`壓入一個值為 a + b 的新節點，`,"with a and b as its children":`以 a 和 b 作為它的孩子`,"return the last node          // the root":`返回 最後一個節點          // 根`,"walk from the root down to the letter:":`從根往下走到這個字母:`,"going left adds a 0, going right a 1":`往左加一個 0，往右加一個 1`,"The codes":`編碼`,"Short codes for common letters":`常用字母用短編碼`,"A message of 13 letters uses only four: A eight times, B three times, C and D once each. Giving every letter a 2-bit code takes 26 bits.":`一條 13 個字母的訊息只用到四個字母：A 八次，B 三次，C 和 D 各一次。給每個字母一個 2 位元編碼，需要 26 位元。`,"It would be shorter if A, which is most of the message, had a 1-bit code. The price is longer codes for the rare letters. <strong>Huffman coding</strong> finds the best trade.":`如果佔了訊息大部分的 A 有一個 1 位元編碼，就會更短。代價是罕見字母的編碼更長。<strong>霍夫曼編碼</strong>能找到最好的取捨。`,"appears 8×":`出現 8 次`,"appears 3×":`出現 3 次`,"appears 1×":`出現 1 次`,"Bits for the message":`訊息所需的位數`,"Two bits each.":`每個兩位元。`,"Join the two rarest":`合併最罕見的兩個`,"Find the two smallest counts: C and D, 1 each. Hang them from a new node worth their sum, 2.":`找出最小的兩個次數：C 和 D，各 1 次。把它們掛在一個新節點下，新節點的值是它們的和 2。`,"From now on that pair is treated as a single item that appears twice.":`從現在起，這一對被當作一個出現兩次的項。`,"Three items are left: A at 8, B at 3 and the pair at 2. The two smallest are B and the pair. Join them under a node worth 5.":`剩下三個項：A 為 8，B 為 3，這一對為 2。最小的兩個是 B 和這一對。把它們合併到一個值為 5 的節點下。`,"C and D have just sunk a level deeper. Every time something is joined, everything under it gets one bit longer.":`C 和 D 剛剛又沉下去一層。每次有東西被合併，它下面的一切都會多一個位元。`,"Until one tree is left":`直到只剩一棵樹`,"Two items left, A at 8 and the node at 5. Join them: 13, the length of the whole message. That node is the root.":`剩下兩個項，A 為 8，節點為 5。合併它們：13，正是整條訊息的長度。這個節點就是根。`,"A was never one of the two smallest, so it was joined last and sits right under the root.":`A 從來不是最小的兩個之一，所以它最後才被合併，就在根的正下方。`,"Read the codes off the branches":`從樹枝上讀出編碼`,"Going left is a 0 and going right is a 1. A letter’s code is the path to it from the root.":`往左是 0，往右是 1。一個字母的編碼就是從根到它的路徑。`,"A is 0. B is 10. C is 110 and D is 111. The message takes 8 × 1 + 3 × 2 + 1 × 3 + 1 × 3 = 20 bits, down from 26.":`A 是 0。B 是 10。C 是 110，D 是 111。訊息需要 8 × 1 + 3 × 2 + 1 × 3 + 1 × 3 = 20 位元，比 26 位元少。`,"Six bits saved on thirteen letters.":`十三個字母省了六個位元。`,"No commas needed":`不需要分隔符`,Decoding:`解碼`,"Letters only ever sit at the ends of branches, so no code is the beginning of another. To decode, start at the root and follow the bits until you land on a letter: 1, 1, 0 is C. Then start again at the root.":`字母只會出現在樹枝的末端，所以沒有一個編碼是另一個編碼的開頭。解碼時，從根開始沿著位元走，直到落在一個字母上：1、1、0 是 C。然後再從根開始。`,"Always joining the two rarest is a greedy rule, and here greedy is provably the best possible.":`總是合併最罕見的兩個是一個貪婪規則，而在這裡，貪婪被證明是最好的。`,"O(n log n) with a min-heap. It is the last stage of ZIP, JPEG and MP3.":`用最小堆積是 O(n log n)。它是 ZIP、JPEG 和 MP3 的最後一個階段。`},"when-greedy-fails":{"while node has children:":`當 node 有孩子:`,"node ← the child with the bigger value":`node ← 值較大的那個孩子`,"return total":`返回 total`,"if node is nothing: return 0":`如果 node 為空: 返回 0`,"return node.value + the larger of":`返回 node.value + 以下兩者中較大的`,"best_walk(node.left) and best_walk(node.right)":`best_walk(node.left) 和 best_walk(node.right)`,"Two walks":`兩種走法`,"Take the best on offer":`拿眼前最好的`,"Every greedy algorithm has the same shape: at each step take whatever looks best right now, and never go back on it. That is what makes them fast, and simple to write.":`每個貪婪演算法都是同一個樣子：每一步都拿現在看起來最好的東西，並且從不反悔。這正是它們快、而且寫起來簡單的原因。`,"Here is a test for the idea. Walk from the top node to the bottom, adding up the numbers you pass. The biggest total wins.":`這裡有一個檢驗這個思路的例子。從最上面的節點走到最底下，把經過的數加起來。總和最大的贏。`,"start with 5":`從 5 開始`,"Greedy path":`貪婪路徑`,"Greedy total":`貪婪總和`,"Best path":`最佳路徑`,"not looked for":`沒有去找`,"Best total":`最佳總和`,"The bigger number":`較大的數`,"Below the top are 7 and 3. Greedy does not hesitate: 7 is bigger. The total is 12.":`最上面的下方是 7 和 3。貪婪毫不猶豫：7 更大。總和是 12。`,"The whole right-hand side of the tree has just been given up, without a look at what is in it.":`整棵樹的右半邊就這樣被放棄了，連看都沒看裡面有什麼。`,"7 beats 3":`7 勝過 3`,"Stuck with what is left":`只能接受剩下的`,"Under 7 the choice is between 1 and 2. Greedy takes 2 and finishes with 14.":`在 7 下面，要在 1 和 2 之間選。貪婪選 2，最後得到 14。`,"Every single choice was the best one available at the time.":`每一個選擇在當時都是可選的最好的一個。`,"total 14":`總和 14`,"What it never saw":`它從沒看到的東西`,Counterexample:`反例`,"Go right at the top instead. 3 looks like the worse choice, but it leads to 9: a total of 17.":`在最上面改為往右走。3 看起來是更差的選擇，但它通向 9：總和 17。`,"Greedy missed it because the 9 was hidden behind a small number. One good-looking choice at the start closed off the best answer for good.":`貪婪錯過了它，因為 9 藏在一個小數後面。開頭一個看起來不錯的選擇，永遠關上了通往最佳答案的門。`,"total 17":`總和 17`,"Looking at everything":`把一切都看一遍`,"To be sure of the best, every path has to be accounted for. Work upwards: the best total from each node is its own number plus the better of its two children’s totals.":`要確定得到最好的，每條路徑都必須考慮到。從下往上做：每個節點出發的最佳總和，是它自己的數加上它兩個孩子的總和中較好的那個。`,"From 7 the best is 9. From 3 it is 12. So from the top it is 5 + 12 = 17. That is dynamic programming, and it looks at every node once.":`從 7 出發最好是 9。從 3 出發是 12。所以從最上面出發是 5 + 12 = 17。這就是動態規劃，每個節點只看一次。`,"When greedy is right":`貪婪什麼時候是對的`,"Greedy is only safe when you can argue that the best-looking choice is always part of <em>some</em> best answer. Earliest finish in interval scheduling passes that test. So do Huffman’s two rarest, and Kruskal’s cheapest edge.":`只有當你能論證看起來最好的選擇總是<em>某個</em>最佳答案的一部分時，貪婪才是安全的。區間排程中的最早結束透過了這個檢驗。霍夫曼的兩個最罕見的、Kruskal 的最便宜的邊也一樣。`,"Giving change with the largest coin first works for 1, 5, 10, 25 and fails for 1, 3, 4. Before trusting a greedy rule, hunt for a small case that breaks it.":`找零時先給最大的硬幣，對 1、5、10、25 有效，對 1、3、4 就不行。在相信一條貪婪規則之前，先找找有沒有能推翻它的小例子。`,"If one turns up":`如果找到了一個`,"Fall back on dynamic programming or backtracking: slower, but they consider every option.":`退回到動態規劃或回溯：慢一些，但它們會考慮每一種選項。`},subsets:t,permutations:n,"n-queens":{"if row is past the last: a solution":`如果 row 超過了最後一行: 找到一個解`,"for each column in this row:":`對每個 這一行中的列:`,"if no queen attacks that square:":`如果 沒有皇后攻擊那個格子:`,"put a queen there":`在那裡放一個皇后`,"take it off again        // backtrack":`再把它拿走        // 回溯`,"Four queens, no attacks":`四個皇后，互不攻擊`,"Put four queens on a 4 × 4 board so that no two share a row, a column or a diagonal.":`在 4 × 4 的棋盤上放四個皇后，使任意兩個都不在同一行、同一列或同一條對角線上。`,"There are 1,820 ways to put four queens on sixteen squares. Backtracking finds a good one by trying almost none of them: one queen per row, and give up on a board the moment it cannot be finished.":`在十六個格子上放四個皇后，有 1,820 种放法。回溯幾乎一種都不用試就能找到一個好的：每行一個皇后，一旦某個棋盤不可能完成就立刻放棄。`,"Queens placed":`已放的皇后`,"Times backed up":`退回的次數`,"Place one, cross out what it attacks":`放一個，劃掉它攻擊的格子`,Place:`放置`,"Put the first queen in the first square of row 1. Cross out every square below that it attacks: its column and its diagonal.":`把第一個皇后放在第 1 行的第一個格子。劃掉它下方能攻擊到的每個格子：它所在的列和對角線。`,"Those squares are ruled out for good, as long as this queen stays.":`只要這個皇后還在，這些格子就永遠排除了。`,"The next row":`下一行`,"Row 2 has two safe squares left. Take the first, c, and cross out what the new queen attacks.":`第 2 行還剩兩個安全的格子。取第一個 c，劃掉新皇后攻擊的格子。`,"A dead end":`死路`,"Dead end":`死路`,"Row 3 has no safe square at all. This board can never be finished, whatever is done in row 4.":`第 3 行一個安全的格子都沒有。不管第 4 行怎麼放，這個棋盤都不可能完成。`,"So nothing more is tried on it. Everything that would have followed is skipped at a stroke: that is the power of backtracking.":`所以不再在它上面嘗試任何東西。原本會接著發生的一切都被一筆勾銷：這就是回溯的威力。`,"nowhere is safe":`沒有安全的地方`,"Step back and try the next":`退一步，試下一個`,"Take the last queen off and try the next square in its row, d. Now row 3 has a safe square, b. But then row 4 has none.":`拿走最後一個皇后，試它所在行的下一個格子 d。現在第 3 行有一個安全的格子 b。但接著第 4 行一個都沒有。`,"Both squares in row 2 have failed. The fault lies further back: with the very first queen.":`第 2 行的兩個格子都失敗了。問題出在更早的地方：就在第一個皇后身上。`,"A solution":`一個解`,"Move the first queen to b and go again: d in row 2, a in row 3, c in row 4. Four queens, none attacking another.":`把第一個皇后移到 b，再來一遍：第 2 行放 d，第 3 行放 a，第 4 行放 c。四個皇后，誰也不攻擊誰。`,"It took a handful of placements, because every dead end was dropped as soon as it showed itself.":`只放了幾次，因為每條死路一出現就被放棄了。`,"The pattern":`模式`,"Choose, check, go deeper; when stuck, undo the last choice and try the next. Sudoku, mazes and timetables are solved the same way.":`選擇、檢查、深入；卡住了就撤銷上一個選擇，試下一個。數獨、迷宮和排課表都是這樣解的。`},maze:r,memoization:i,tabulation:a,"grid-paths":{"for r from 1 to rows − 1:":`對於 r 從 1 到 rows − 1:`,"for c from 1 to cols − 1:":`對於 c 從 1 到 cols − 1:`,"return ways[last r][last c]":`返回 ways[最後的 r][最後的 c]`,"Only right, only down":`只能向右，只能向前`,"A robot stands on the back-left square of a 3 × 4 grid. It can step one square right or one square forward, never back. How many different routes take it to the opposite corner?":`一個機器人站在 3 × 4 網格左後方的格子上。它每步可以向右或向前走一格，從不後退。有多少條不同的路線能把它帶到對角？`,"Start with what is certain: there is exactly one way to be where it already is.":`先從確定的開始：待在它已經在的地方，正好有一種方式。`,start:`起點`,Grid:`網格`,"Squares filled":`已填格子`,"Routes to the far corner":`到對角的路線數`,"The edges are easy":`邊上很簡單`,"Along the back row the robot can only have kept going right. Along the left column it can only have kept coming forward.":`沿著最後面那一排，機器人只可能一直向右走。沿著最左邊那一列，它只可能一直向前走。`,"One route to each of those squares.":`到這些格子都只有一條路線。`,"Arrive from behind or from the left":`從後面或從左邊來`,"Any other square can be entered in only two ways: from the square behind it, or from the square to its left.":`其他任何格子都只有兩種進入方式：從它後面的格子，或者從它左邊的格子。`,"So the routes to it are the routes to those two, added together. For this square, 1 + 1 = 2.":`所以到它的路線數，就是到這兩個格子的路線數之和。對這個格子來說，1 + 1 = 2。`,"Fill the row":`填滿這一排`,"Carry on along the row. Each square adds the one behind it and the one to its left, both already filled in.":`沿著這一排繼續。每個格子把它後面的和左邊的加起來，兩個都已經填好了。`,"2 + 1 = 3, then 3 + 1 = 4.":`2 + 1 = 3，然後 3 + 1 = 4。`,"The far corner":`對角`,"The front row goes the same way: 3, then 6, then the corner: 4 from behind plus 6 from the left.":`最前面一排也一樣：3，然後 6，然後是對角：後面的 4 加上左邊的 6。`,"Ten routes.":`十條路線。`,"One table, many questions":`一張表，很多問題`,"Each square was filled once, from two neighbours. The same table handles the usual twists.":`每個格子只填一次，由兩個鄰居得出。同一張表還能處理常見的變化。`,"A blocked square simply gets 0. If squares have costs and you want the cheapest route, take the <em>smaller</em> of the two neighbours instead of adding them.":`被擋住的格子直接填 0。如果格子有代價，而你想要最便宜的路線，就取兩個鄰居中<em>較小</em>的那個，而不是把它們相加。`,"O(rows × columns) time. Only the previous row is ever read, so one row of memory is enough.":`O(行數 × 列數) 時間。只會讀取前一行，所以一行的記憶體就夠了。`},knapsack:o,"coin-change":{"for a from 1 to amount:":`對於 a 從 1 到 amount:`,"fewest[a] ← 1 + the smallest of fewest[a − c],":`fewest[a] ← 1 + fewest[a − c] 中最小的，`,"over every coin c that is not bigger than a":`c 取所有不大於 a 的硬幣`,"return fewest[amount]":`返回 fewest[amount]`,"Making change":`找零`,"When greedy goes wrong":`貪婪出錯的時候`,"With coins worth 1, 3 and 4, what is the fewest needed to make 6? The obvious method, biggest coin first, gives 4 + 1 + 1: three coins. But 3 + 3 does it in two.":`用面值 1、3 和 4 的硬幣，湊出 6 最少需要幾枚？顯而易見的方法是先用最大的硬幣，得到 4 + 1 + 1：三枚。但 3 + 3 只要兩枚。`,"Being greedy does not always work. Dynamic programming does: work out the answer for every smaller amount first. Making 0 takes no coins.":`貪婪並不總是管用。動態規劃管用：先算出每個更小金額的答案。湊出 0 不需要硬幣。`,Coins:`硬幣`,Amount:`金額`,"Fewest coins":`最少硬幣數`,"Build up from below":`從下往上搭`,"For 1 and 2, only the 1-coin fits. So the answer is one coin plus the answer for one less.":`對 1 和 2，只有 1 元硬幣放得進去。所以答案是一枚硬幣加上少一元時的答案。`,"Try every last coin":`試遍每種最後一枚硬幣`,"For 3 there is a choice. If the last coin is a 1, the rest is 2, which needs two coins: three in all. If the last coin is a 3, the rest is 0: one coin.":`對 3 就有選擇了。如果最後一枚是 1，剩下的是 2，需要兩枚：一共三枚。如果最後一枚是 3，剩下的是 0：一枚。`,"Whatever the best way is, it ends with <em>some</em> coin. Try each, and keep the best.":`不管最好的方法是什麼，它都以<em>某枚</em>硬幣結束。每種都試一下，保留最好的。`,"Each cell reads back":`每個格子都往回讀`,"4 is a single coin. 5 looks back by 1, by 3 and by 4, at the cells for 4, 2 and 1, and takes the smallest: 4 and then 1.":`4 是單獨一枚硬幣。5 往回看 1、3 和 4，也就是 4、2 和 1 的格子，取最小的：4 然後 1。`,"Every cell is filled the same way, from cells already known.":`每個格子都是用同樣的方法，從已知的格子填出來的。`,"The case greedy missed":`貪婪錯過的情況`,"6 looks back at 5, 3 and 2, which need 2, 1 and 2 coins. The best is through 3: one more coin makes two. That is 3 + 3.":`6 往回看 5、3 和 2，它們分別需要 2、1 和 2 枚。最好的是經過 3：再加一枚就是兩枚。也就是 3 + 3。`,"Nothing was assumed about which coin is best. Every option was simply checked.":`沒有預設哪枚硬幣最好。每個選項都只是檢查了一遍。`,"Greedy would have used three.":`貪婪會用三枚。`,"Any amount":`任意金額`,"7 is two coins as well, 3 + 4. The table can go on as far as is needed.":`7 也是兩枚，3 + 4。這張表需要多長都可以繼續下去。`,"A greedy choice is quick and sometimes wrong. A table of subproblems is a little slower and always right.":`貪婪的選擇很快，有時會錯。子問題表稍微慢一點，但總是對的。`,"O(amount × number of coins).":`O(金額 × 硬幣種類數)。`},"longest-increasing-subsequence":{"for each j before i:":`對每個 i 之前的 j:`,"if a[j] < a[i]:":`如果 a[j] < a[i]:`,"longest[i] ← the larger of":`longest[i] ← 以下兩者中較大的`,"longest[i] and longest[j] + 1":`longest[i] 和 longest[j] + 1`,"return the largest value in longest":`返回 longest 中的最大值`,"Rising, with gaps allowed":`遞增，允許跳過`,"Pick numbers from this row, left to right, so that each is bigger than the one before. You may skip as many as you like. How long can the run be?":`從這一排裡從左到右挑數，讓每個都比前一個大。想跳過多少個都行。這串數最長能有多長？`,"3, 4, 5 is one such run. Trying every possible selection means 2ⁿ of them.":`3、4、5 就是這樣的一串。試遍每種可能的挑法，就是 2ⁿ 種。`,"The numbers":`這些數`,"of 5":`/ 5`,"The best run ending here":`以這裡結尾的最長一串`,"Ask a smaller question of each cell: what is the longest rising run that <strong>ends at this number</strong>?":`對每個格子問一個更小的問題：<strong>以這個數結尾</strong>的最長遞增串有多長？`,"For 3 it is just itself: 1. For 1 there is nothing smaller before it to follow, so also 1.":`對 3 來說，就是它自己：1。對 1 來說，它前面沒有更小的數可以接在後面，所以也是 1。`,"nothing smaller before":`前面沒有更小的`,"Follow something smaller":`接在更小的後面`,"4 can come after any smaller number to its left. Both 3 and 1 are smaller, and each ends a run of length 1.":`4 可以接在它左邊任何一個更小的數後面。3 和 1 都更小，而且各自都結束一串長度為 1 的。`,"Follow either one and the run is 1 + 1 = 2.":`接在任何一個後面，這一串都是 1 + 1 = 2。`,"Only the smaller ones count":`只有更小的才算`,"2 cannot follow 3 or 4: they are bigger. It can follow 1, which gives 1 + 1 = 2.":`2 不能接在 3 或 4 後面：它們更大。它可以接在 1 後面，得到 1 + 1 = 2。`,"after 1 only":`只能接在 1 後面`,"Take the best of them":`取其中最好的`,"5 is bigger than everything before it, so it can follow any of them. The best runs to follow are the two of length 2.":`5 比它前面的所有數都大，所以可以接在任何一個後面。可接的最好的串是那兩個長度為 2 的。`,"The biggest number in the row":`這一排中最大的數`,"The answer is the largest value in the back row: 3. It need not be in the last cell.":`答案是後面一排裡的最大值：3。它不一定在最後一個格子裡。`,"One such run is 3, 4, 5. Each cell looked back at every cell before it: two loops, one inside the other.":`這樣的一串是 3、4、5。每個格子都回頭看了它前面的每個格子：兩重迴圈，一個套在另一個裡面。`,"O(n²) like this. A cleverer version with binary search gets it down to O(n log n).":`這樣做是 O(n²)。用二分搜尋的更巧妙的版本能把它降到 O(n log n)。`,"One longest run: 3, 4, 5.":`一個最長的串：3、4、5。`},sequences:s,"edit-distance":{"for each i, and each j:":`對每個 i 和每個 j:`,"edits[i][j] ← 1 + the smallest of":`edits[i][j] ← 1 + 以下三者中最小的`,"edits[i − 1][j]         // delete":`edits[i − 1][j]         // 刪除`,"edits[i][j − 1]         // insert":`edits[i][j − 1]         // 插入`,"edits[i − 1][j − 1]     // replace":`edits[i − 1][j − 1]     // 替換`,"return edits[last i][last j]":`返回 edits[最後的 i][最後的 j]`,"How far apart are two words?":`兩個詞相差多遠？`,"Turn SEA into EAT using three kinds of change: delete a letter, insert a letter, or replace one with another. The fewest changes needed is the <strong>edit distance</strong>.":`用三種修改把 SEA 變成 EAT：刪除一個字母、插入一個字母，或者把一個字母替換成另一個。所需的最少修改次數就是<strong>編輯距離</strong>。`,"The table has a cell for every pair of beginnings. The edges are easy: turning nothing into EAT takes three inserts, and turning SEA into nothing takes three deletes.":`這張表為每一對開頭部分準備了一個格子。邊上很簡單：從空變成 EAT 要插入三次，從 SEA 變成空要刪除三次。`,"Spell checkers, “did you mean…”, comparing files, matching DNA.":`拼寫檢查器、「你是不是要找……」、檔案比較、DNA 比對。`,From:`從`,To:`到`,"Edits needed":`需要的修改次數`,"When the letters differ":`字母不同時`,"S into E. The letters differ, so one change is needed, on top of the cheapest of three smaller problems: the cell above (delete), the cell to the left (insert), or the cell diagonally back (replace).":`S 變成 E。字母不同，所以需要一次修改，再加上三個更小問題中最便宜的那個：上面的格子（刪除）、左邊的格子（插入），或者斜後方的格子（替換）。`,"The cheapest of those is 0, so the answer is 1: replace S with E.":`其中最便宜的是 0，所以答案是 1：把 S 替換成 E。`,"When they match":`字母相同時`,"SE into E. The last letters are the same, so that letter costs nothing. The answer is whatever it took before it: the cell diagonally back, 1.":`SE 變成 E。最後的字母相同，所以這個字母不花任何代價。答案就是它之前所需的：斜後方的格子，1。`,"That 1 was “delete the S”, and it still is.":`那個 1 是「刪除 S」，現在仍然是。`,"E = E: still 1":`E = E：仍是 1`,"The whole table":`整張表`,"The last cell covers both whole words. A and T differ, so it is 1 plus the smallest of its three neighbours, which is the 1 to its left.":`最後一個格子涵蓋兩個完整的詞。A 和 T 不同，所以它是 1 加上三個鄰居中最小的，也就是它左邊的 1。`,"SEA becomes EAT in two changes.":`SEA 經過兩次修改變成 EAT。`,"Which two changes":`哪兩次修改`,"Walk back from the corner, each time to the cell the answer came from. A step left is an insert, a step up a delete, a diagonal step a match or a replace.":`從角上往回走，每次都走到答案來自的那個格子。往左一步是插入，往上一步是刪除，斜著一步是匹配或替換。`,"Left: insert T. Then two matches, A and E. Then up: delete S. Two changes, and the table has said which.":`往左：插入 T。然後兩次匹配，A 和 E。然後往上：刪除 S。兩次修改，而表已經說明了是哪兩次。`,"delete S, insert T":`刪除 S，插入 T`},"bits-and-masks":{"mask ← only bit k switched on":`mask ← 只開啟第 k 位元`,"return (x AND mask) is not 0":`返回 (x AND mask) 是否不為 0`,"return x OR mask":`返回 x OR mask`,"return x AND (NOT mask)":`返回 x AND (NOT mask)`,"return x XOR mask":`返回 x XOR mask`,"A number is a row of switches":`數字是一排開關`,"Inside the machine every number is a row of <strong>bits</strong>: switches that are on or off. Each is worth twice the one to its right: 1, 2, 4, 8 and so on.":`在機器內部，每個數字都是一排<strong>位元</strong>：開著或關著的開關。每個位元的值都是它右邊那個位元的兩倍：1、2、4、8，依此類推。`,"A block means the bit is on. Here that is 32, 8, 4 and 1, so this byte holds 45. The empty row behind is for a second number.":`方塊表示這個位元是開著的。這裡是 32、8、4 和 1，所以這個位元組存的是 45。後面那一排空的是給第二個數用的。`,mask:`遮罩`,"A mask points at one bit":`遮罩指向一個位元`,Test:`檢查`,"To ask about a single bit, make a second number with only that bit on: a <strong>mask</strong>.":`要問某個位元的情況，就做第二個數，只開啟那個位元：這就是<strong>遮罩</strong>。`,"<strong>AND</strong> keeps a bit only where both rows have one. The 8 bit is on in both, so something survives: the bit is set.":`<strong>AND</strong> 只在兩排都有的地方保留一個位元。8 這個位元在兩排裡都開著，所以有東西留下來：這個位元已設定。`,"on in both":`兩排都開著`,"not 0: the bit is on":`不為 0：這個位元是開著的`,"OR switches a bit on":`OR 開啟一個位元`,"Now a mask with only the 64 bit. <strong>OR</strong> gives a 1 wherever either row has one.":`現在是一個只有 64 這個位元的遮罩。<strong>OR</strong> 在任意一排有 1 的地方都給出 1。`,"The 64 bit comes on and nothing else is touched. 45 becomes 109.":`64 這個位元開啟了，其他什麼都沒碰。45 變成 109。`,"AND with the opposite switches it off":`和反面做 AND 就把它關掉`,Clear:`清除`,"To switch the 4 bit off, the mask is turned inside out: every bit on <em>except</em> the 4. Then AND.":`要關掉 4 這個位元，就把遮罩裡外翻轉：除了 4 <em>以外</em>的每個位元都開啟。然後做 AND。`,"Every block in front has one behind it apart from the 4, so that is the only one to go. 109 becomes 105.":`前面每個方塊後面都有一個，只有 4 沒有，所以只有它被去掉。109 變成 105。`,"XOR flips":`XOR 翻轉`,Toggle:`切換`,"<strong>XOR</strong> gives a 1 where the two rows differ. Wherever the mask has a 1, the bit in front turns over.":`<strong>XOR</strong> 在兩排不同的地方給出 1。遮罩中是 1 的地方，前面那個位元就會翻轉。`,"This mask has the 2 and the 1. The 2 bit comes on, the 1 bit goes off. 105 becomes 106.":`這個遮罩有 2 和 1。2 這個位元開啟，1 這個位元關掉。105 變成 106。`,"both flipped":`兩個位元都翻轉了`,"Eight answers in a byte":`一個位元組裡的八個答案`,"Each of these is a single machine instruction, and takes the same time whatever the number.":`這些操作每個都只是一條機器指令，不管數字是多少，花的時間都一樣。`,"That makes bits ideal for flags: file permissions, feature switches, which keys are held down. One 64-bit number holds sixty-four yes-or-no answers.":`這讓位元非常適合做標誌：檔案權限、功能開關、哪些鍵被按住了。一個 64 位元的數能存六十四個「是或否」的答案。`,"O(1) for every operation here.":`這裡的每個操作都是 O(1)。`,Set:`設定`},"bit-tricks":{"return x << 1":`返回 x << 1`,"return x >> 1":`返回 x >> 1`,"while x is not 0:":`當 x 不為 0:`,"x ← x AND (x − 1)     // drops the lowest 1":`x ← x AND (x − 1)     // 去掉最低的 1`,"return x is not 0 and (x AND (x − 1)) = 0":`返回 x 不為 0 且 (x AND (x − 1)) = 0`,"Every place is worth double":`每個位元的值都是兩倍`,"This is 5: the 4 bit and the 1 bit. Each place in the row is worth twice the place to its right.":`這是 5：4 這個位元和 1 這個位元。這一排中每個位置的值都是它右邊位置的兩倍。`,"So moving the bits along the row does arithmetic. The row behind is spare for now.":`所以沿著這一排移動這些位元就是在做算術。後面那一排暫時空著。`,Trick:`技巧`,Gives:`得到`,"Shift left to double":`左移就是翻倍`,"<strong>x &lt;&lt; 1</strong> slides every bit one place to the left. Each lands on a place worth twice as much, so the whole number doubles: 10.":`<strong>x &lt;&lt; 1</strong> 把每個位元向左滑一個位置。每個位元都落到值是兩倍的位置上，所以整個數翻倍：10。`,"Shifting k places multiplies by 2ᵏ.":`移動 k 個位置就是乘以 2ᵏ。`,"Shift right to halve":`右移就是減半`,"<strong>x &gt;&gt; 1</strong> slides everything back to the right. Every bit is worth half what it was: 10 becomes 5.":`<strong>x &gt;&gt; 1</strong> 把所有位元滑回右邊。每個位元的值都是原來的一半：10 變成 5。`,"What falls off the end":`從末端掉下去的東西`,"Shift right once more. The 1 bit has nowhere to go, and is dropped. 5 becomes 2: halved, with the remainder thrown away.":`再右移一次。1 這個位元無處可去，被丟掉了。5 變成 2：減半，餘數扔掉。`,"That last bit says whether a number is odd. <strong>x AND 1</strong> reads it, and is the quickest odd-or-even test there is.":`最後這個位元說明一個數是不是奇數。<strong>x AND 1</strong> 讀取它，這是最快的奇偶檢查。`,"The remainder, 1, is lost.":`餘數 1 丟掉了。`,"One less than a number":`比一個數少一`,"A new number: 12, which is 8 + 4. Behind it stands 12 − 1 = 11.":`一個新數：12，也就是 8 + 4。它後面站著 12 − 1 = 11。`,"Subtracting 1 always does the same thing to the bits. The lowest 1 goes off, and every 0 below it comes on. Everything above stays as it was.":`減去 1 對這些位元做的事總是一樣的。最低的 1 關掉，它下面的每個 0 都開啟。上面的一切保持原樣。`,"the lowest 1":`最低的 1`,"AND them, and the lowest 1 is gone":`把它們 AND 起來，最低的 1 就沒了`,"Now <strong>x AND (x − 1)</strong>. Above the lowest 1 the two rows match, so those bits survive. From the lowest 1 down they never both have a block.":`現在做 <strong>x AND (x − 1)</strong>。在最低的 1 上面，兩排是一樣的，所以那些位元保留下來。從最低的 1 往下，兩排從不同時有方塊。`,"Exactly one bit disappears: 12 becomes 8.":`正好消失一個位元：12 變成 8。`,"Two things that buys":`這能帶來的兩樣好處`,"To count the 1s in a number, keep knocking off the lowest until nothing is left. The loop runs once per 1, not once per bit.":`要數一個數裡有幾個 1，就不斷去掉最低的那個，直到什麼都不剩。迴圈每個 1 跑一次，而不是每個位元跑一次。`,"A power of two has exactly one bit on. So x is a power of two when knocking that bit off leaves 0, as it would here.":`2 的冪恰好只有一個位元是開著的。所以當去掉那個位元後剩下 0 時，x 就是 2 的冪，就像這裡這樣。`,"Compilers already turn × 2 and ÷ 2 into shifts. Write the arithmetic you mean, and keep these for when bits are the point.":`編譯器本來就會把 × 2 和 ÷ 2 變成移位。寫出你想表達的算術，把這些技巧留到真正和位元打交道的時候用。`,"So 8 is a power of two.":`所以 8 是 2 的冪。`},bitsets:c,"p-vs-np":{"total ← add up the roads along the route":`total ← 把路線上的道路加起來`,"return total ≤ budget          // one pass: quick":`返回 total ≤ budget          // 一趟：很快`,"best ← nothing":`best ← 空`,"for each order the towns could be visited in:":`對每個 訪問這些城鎮可能的順序:`,"if that round trip is cheaper than best:":`如果 這一圈比 best 便宜:`,"best ← that round trip":`best ← 這一圈`,"return best                    // every order: hopeless":`返回 best                    // 每種順序：沒希望`,"The round":`這一圈`,"A delivery round":`一圈送貨路線`,"A van leaves A, has to call at every town once, and come home. Which order makes the cheapest round trip?":`一輛貨車從 A 出發，必須到每個城鎮各一次，然後回家。哪種順序的一圈最便宜？`,"It sounds like a shortest-path problem, and those were easy. This one is the <strong>travelling salesman problem</strong>, and it is not.":`這聽起來像最短路徑問題，而那些都很容易。這個是<strong>旅行商問題</strong>，它可不容易。`,Route:`路線`,"Round trips possible":`可能的環路數`,"for 4 towns":`對 4 個城鎮`,"Checking an answer is quick":`檢查一個答案很快`,Check:`檢查`,"Someone hands you a route: A, D, B, C and home. Is it a round trip costing 21 or less? Follow it and add up: 3 + 2 + 7 + 9 = 21. Yes.":`有人給你一條路線：A、D、B、C，然後回家。它是一圈花費 21 或更少的路線嗎？沿著它走，加起來：3 + 2 + 7 + 9 = 21。是的。`,"One pass along the route settles it. Checking a proposed answer is fast however many towns there are.":`沿著路線走一趟就解決了。檢查一個給出的答案很快，不管有多少個城鎮。`,"total 21":`總計 21`,"Finding the best is not":`找出最好的卻不快`,"That route went to the nearest town each time, and it is not the best. Round the outside, A, B, C, D and home, costs 4 + 7 + 6 + 3 = 20.":`那條路線每次都去最近的城鎮，而它不是最好的。沿著外圈走，A、B、C、D，然後回家，花費 4 + 7 + 6 + 3 = 20。`,"How do you know 20 cannot be beaten? Only by ruling out every other order. Every known method that guarantees the best answer takes time that explodes as towns are added.":`你怎麼知道 20 不能被超越？只有把其他每種順序都排除掉。每種保證得到最佳答案的已知方法，所需時間都會隨著城鎮的增加而爆炸。`,"total 20":`總計 20`,"The count explodes":`數量爆炸`,"Four towns have only 3 different round trips. Each extra town multiplies the count: 12 for five towns, 181,440 for ten.":`四個城鎮只有 3 種不同的環路。每多一個城鎮，數量就會成倍增加：五個城鎮 12 種，十個城鎮 181,440 種。`,"At twenty towns there are sixty million billion. A machine checking a billion routes a second would need about two years. At thirty towns, far longer than the age of the universe.":`二十個城鎮時有六京種。一臺每秒檢查十億條路線的機器大約需要兩年。三十個城鎮時，所需時間遠遠超過宇宙的年齡。`,"4 towns":`4 個城鎮`,"3 round trips":`3 種環路`,"5 towns":`5 個城鎮`,"10 towns":`10 個城鎮`,"15 towns":`15 個城鎮`,"43.6 billion":`436 億`,"20 towns":`20 個城鎮`,"60 million billion":`6 京`,"(n − 1)! ÷ 2 round trips for n towns.":`n 個城鎮有 (n − 1)! ÷ 2 種環路。`,"P and NP":`P 與 NP`,"<strong>P</strong> is the class of problems that can be <em>solved</em> in polynomial time: n, n², n³. Sorting, shortest paths, spanning trees: almost everything in this course.":`<strong>P</strong> 是能在多項式時間內<em>解出</em>的問題類：n、n²、n³。排序、最短路徑、生成樹：這門課裡幾乎所有東西。`,"<strong>NP</strong> is the class whose answers can be <em>checked</em> in polynomial time. “Is there a round trip costing 20 or less?” is in NP. Everything in P is in NP too. Whether the two classes are really the same, whether quick to check always means quick to solve, is the most famous open question in computing.":`<strong>NP</strong> 是答案能在多項式時間內<em>驗證</em>的問題類。「有沒有花費 20 或更少的環路？」屬於 NP。P 中的一切也都屬於 NP。這兩類是否真的相同，也就是「驗證快」是否總意味著「求解快」，是計算機領域最著名的懸而未決的問題。`,Unsolved:`未解決`,"Almost everyone believes P ≠ NP. No one has proved it. There is a million-dollar prize.":`幾乎所有人都相信 P ≠ NP。沒有人證明過。為此設有一百萬美元的獎金。`,"Knowing when to stop looking":`知道什麼時候該停止尋找`,"The hardest problems in NP are called <strong>NP-complete</strong>: a fast method for any one of them would give a fast method for all. This round trip question is one. So are timetabling, packing, colouring a map, and Sudoku on large grids.":`NP 中最難的問題叫作 <strong>NP 完全</strong>問題：其中任何一個有了快速方法，所有問題就都有了快速方法。這個環路問題就是其中之一。排課表、裝箱、地圖著色、大棋盤上的數獨也都是。`,"When a problem turns out to be one of these, stop hunting for a fast exact algorithm. Use backtracking or dynamic programming if the input is small, or settle for a method that gets close to the best quickly.":`當一個問題被證明是其中之一時，就別再找快速的精確演算法了。輸入小的話就用回溯或動態規劃，或者退而求其次，用一種能很快接近最佳答案的方法。`,"The knapsack table from earlier is fast only while the capacity is a small number.":`前面那張揹包表，只有在容量是個小數字時才快。`}};export{c as bitsets,l as default,o as knapsack,r as maze,i as memoization,n as permutations,e as quickselect,s as sequences,t as subsets,a as tabulation};